  "raw": {
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005416&lang=en": {
      "title": "School of Business Part-time Teaching Position in Business Analytics and Operations",
      "description": "Job Description - School of Business Part-time Teaching Position in Business Analytics and Operations (26005416) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - School of Business Part-time Teaching Position in Business Analytics and Operations (26005416) Job Description School of Business Part-time Teaching Position in Business Analytics and Operations BUS-Grad Business Administration - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005416 ) The Business Analytics and Operations Area at the School of Business invites applications from qualified candidates for a part-time faculty position for Spring 2027. We seek an experienced professional to teach a web-based graduate-level course in Strategic Procurement and Sourcing. About the Course This 7-week graduate course (Thursday evenings, March 18 – April 29, 2027) examines the strategic role of purchasing and supply management in driving efficient, competitive supply chain operations. Students explore how organizations identify, evaluate, and develop supplier relationships; acquire materials and services at optimal cost and quality; and implement sourcing strategies that ensure a reliable flow of goods. The course emphasizes the impact of procurement decisions on organizational performance, competitiveness, and profitability, while also addressing the legal, ethical, and sustainability considerations that inform effective purchasing practices. Additional qualifications include: Required: Professional experience leading procurement and/or sourcing organizations. Strong written and verbal communication skills developed in a business or corporate setting Experience interacting with graduate students in an academic or professional training environment Preferred: Prior teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level A Graduate degree in Business or Engineering from an AACSB-accredited institution Duties and Responsibilities: Deliver graduate-level instruction on Thursdays, 6:20–9:20 PM, online through the school’s internet teaching platform (ZOOM or TEAMS). Manage course content, assignments, and grades through Canvas (the university’s LMS) Hold office hours (via ZOOM or TEAMS) to support student learning outside the classroom Provide timely, constructive feedback through graded assignments, in-class reviews, and participation Maintain accurate records of student attendance, progress, and performance Interested applicants should submit a resume highlighting academic credentials, relevant business expertise, and any prior teaching experience. We welcome applications from experienced professionals who have hands-on experience in purchasing or supply management with a talent for translating complex sourcing strategies into engaging, practical classroom discussions. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=25005903&lang=en": {
      "title": "Clinical Nursing Faculty - Part-time, Non-tenure Stream",
      "description": "Job Description - Clinical Nursing Faculty - Part-time, Non-tenure Stream (25005903) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Clinical Nursing Faculty - Part-time, Non-tenure Stream (25005903) Job Description Clinical Nursing Faculty - Part-time, Non-tenure Stream Nurs-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 25005903 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing is seeking qualified applicants for part-time, non-tenure stream clinical faculty in the following areas: · Community Health Nursing · Medical/Surgical Nursing · Obstetric Nursing · Pediatric Nursing · Psychiatric/Mental Health Nursing Minimum Qualifications : Instructor of Practice* must have a bachelor’s degree in nursing. Clinical Instructor must have a graduate degree in nursing. Candidates at all faculty ranks must: · Show evidence of or potential for excellence in clinical and/or classroom teaching and contributing to a learning environment that values evidence-based practice; · Demonstrated expertise in at least one of the indicated areas of community health, medical/surgical, obstetric, pediatric, or psychiatric/mental health nursing; · Hold an unencumbered RN license in Pennsylvania or compact state. *If the incumbent has not earned a graduate degree in nursing, the incumbent is required to complete a graduate degree in nursing within five years of the date of hire. Desired Qualifications: Prior experience in clinical education and/or scholarship is preferred but not required. As part of your application, please provide a statement about your area of clinical practice, and why you believe you will be successful at Pitt Nursing. Salary and academic rank are commensurate with qualifications and experience. About the University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing : Since its founding in 1939, the University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing has provided faculty and students with the resources and support to generate new healthcare knowledge and the educational foundation to conduct evidence-based practice, engage in scholarly activities, and translate knowledge to improve the delivery of healthcare in Pennsylvania, the nation, and throughout the world. As one of the nation's elite schools of nursing, Pitt Nursing receives millions of dollars in NIH grant funding each year, and U.S. News & World Report highly ranks multiple academic programs. A complete list of rankings for the School of Nursing can be found at: www.nursing.pitt.edu/about/our-rankings . About the University of Pittsburgh: Named a “New Ivy” by Forbes, the University of Pittsburgh is internationally recognized as a center of learning, innovation, and research. Pitt shares a campus with the world-class healthcare enterprise, UPMC. Collaboration between Pitt and UPMC results in an environment of interdisciplinary research and education, cutting-edge evidence-based practice, and an infrastructure that fosters career development and sustained successes. Reasons to work at Pitt: The University offers exceptional benefits that include education benefits, health and wellness benefits, and a generous retirement plan. There are also generous tuition and educational benefits. Information about these and other benefits can be found on the University’s HR website: https://www.hr.pitt.edu/current-employees/benefits . Apply Now: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Candidates should apply online at https://www.join.pitt.edu/ and search for requisition number: 25005903. For more information on the School of Nursing, visit www.nursing.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006254&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26006254) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26006254) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006254 ) The School of Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking full-time faculty at the level of Associate Professor or Professor with tenure or in the tenure stream. Qualified applicants will be a proven leader in bioethics scholarship, with a track record of excellence in empirically grounded and/or conceptual research, extramural funding, and academic, clinical, or policy leadership. It is anticipated that an endowed chair will be established for this position. All nominations to endowed chairs and professorships to be held by the School of Medicine faculty require review and approval by the standing committee review process. Review is mandatory prior to awarding any endowed chair or professorship. As Professor or Associate Professor , the incumbent will hold a leadership role within the Institute for Bioethics alongside their appointment in the School of Medicine, to be determined based on applicant qualifications and interest. Core responsibilities include building and sustaining an independent program of bioethics research; contributing to mentorship and teaching within the School of Medicine department as appropriate to background and rank; and directing or co-directing one or more of the Institute's research or educational initiatives, with latitude to propose and launch new programs aligned with the incumbent's expertise. The Institute for Bioethics advances research in bioethics and the health humanities, educates the next generation of clinicians, scholars, and leaders in ethical practice, and fosters a community of interprofessional inquiry addressing pressing ethical challenges in healthcare and research. The Institute is the University's principal hub for bioethics and health humanities scholarship, education, and innovation. Its work spans six initiatives that reach across the University: Ethics Education; Education and Programming for Undergraduates; Health Humanities and Social Sciences; Humanistic Communication and Shared Decision Making; Research Ethics; and Clinical Ethics, each anchored by dedicated faculty leadership and active programming across multiple schools. We welcome applicants from any relevant disciplinary background. This is a senior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Candidates holding an MD will be expected to be BC/BE (Board Certified/Board Eligible) physicians or physician-scientists. Candidates holding a PhD or equivalent terminal degree in a relevant discipline (e.g., philosophy, bioethics, health policy, law) are strongly encouraged to apply. Rank-Specific Qualifications Applicants for Associate Professor should have five or more years of experience in related scientific or scholarly research; have independent, external research funding and a substantial record of peer-reviewed publications in bioethics or a closely related discipline; have significant teaching experience; and demonstrate the capacity for sustained, impactful, and independent scholarly contributions and leadership in bioethics. Applicants for Professor should have an extensive record of independent, external research funding and a distinguished record of peer-reviewed publications in bioethics or a closely related discipline; have significant teaching, mentoring, and leadership experience; and demonstrate sustained national or international recognition for scholarly contributions to bioethics. Qualified applicants should apply through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center at join.pitt.edu, requisition # 26006254 . The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006392&lang=en": {
