ip and teaching within the School of Medicine department as appropriate to background and rank; and directing or co-directing one or more of the Institute's research or educational initiatives, with latitude to propose and launch new programs aligned with the incumbent's expertise. The Institute for Bioethics advances research in bioethics and the health humanities, educates the next generation of clinicians, scholars, and leaders in ethical practice, and fosters a community of interprofessional inquiry addressing pressing ethical challenges in healthcare and research. The Institute is the University's principal hub for bioethics and health humanities scholarship, education, and innovation. Its work spans six initiatives that reach across the University: Ethics Education; Education and Programming for Undergraduates; Health Humanities and Social Sciences; Humanistic Communication and Shared Decision Making; Research Ethics; and Clinical Ethics, each anchored by dedicated faculty leadership and active programming across multiple schools. We welcome applicants from any relevant disciplinary background. This is a senior appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Candidates holding an MD will be expected to be BC/BE (Board Certified/Board Eligible) physicians or physician-scientists. Candidates holding a PhD or equivalent terminal degree in a relevant discipline (e.g., philosophy, bioethics, health policy, law) are strongly encouraged to apply. Rank-Specific Qualifications Applicants for Associate Professor should have five or more years of experience in related scientific or scholarly research; have independent, external research funding and a substantial record of peer-reviewed publications in bioethics or a closely related discipline; have significant teaching experience; and demonstrate the capacity for sustained, impactful, and independent scholarly contributions and leadership in bioethics. Applicants for Professor should have an extensive record of independent, external research funding and a distinguished record of peer-reviewed publications in bioethics or a closely related discipline; have significant teaching, mentoring, and leadership experience; and demonstrate sustained national or international recognition for scholarly contributions to bioethics. Qualified applicants should apply through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center at join.pitt.edu, requisition # 26006392 . The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
