    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006104&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26006104) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26006104) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006104 ) The UPMC Heart and Vascular Institute is recruiting a full-time board-certified or board-eligible Cardiology/Critical Care Medicine physician at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Professor, open tenure to join our expanding team! The successful candidate will practice in a dual capacity within the UPMC Heart and Vascular Institute (HVI) and the University of Pittsburgh Department of Medicine Division of Cardiology to include clinical, research and teaching responsibilities. He/she will participate in outreach efforts for the HVI, expanding inpatient and outpatient activities at locations within the HVI service area. As a faculty member, the successful candidate will actively participate in the research and educational mission of the HVI. Job duties include general cardiology coverage in both the inpatient and outpatient setting, including clinical coverage in the Cardiac Intensive Care Unit (CCU) and Cardiothoracic Intensive Care Unit (CTICU), and potentially in the cardiology consultative services, ECG analysis, interpretation of transthoracic echocardiograms and performance and interpretation of transesophageal echocardiograms and cardiac nuclear studies as needed or as desired by the applicant. These duties will be performed in rotation with other cardiologists within the practice. After-hours and weekend cardiology coverage will be shared among the group. Requirements: The ideal candidate will possess the following qualifications: - Experience as a teacher or mentor of medical students and residents - Board Certified or board eligible in Cardiology and Critical Care - Demonstrated excellent clinic outcomes - Qualified for medical licensure in Pennsylvania - Applicants who will have completed training will also be considered Licensure, Certifications and Clearances: - Pennsylvania medical license, American Board Certification An Assistant Professor should have at least 3 years of experience in teaching, in advanced study and research, or professional experience of a kind which would enable them to make an academic contribution. The Assistant Professor should possess a doctoral or appropriate professional degree in the field of cardiology. The Associate Professor will have served a minimum of 5 years as an Assistant Professor. An Associate Professor will have a strong experience with an impactful scholarship, a local, regional, and developing national reputation, effectiveness as a teacher, and service. For Professor level, most individuals will have served 5 to 7 years as Associate Professor. Professor level should have attained superior stature in their field through scholarship, professional practice, and leadership in professional and learned organizations. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae for position #26006104 and apply using this link: http://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005879&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26005879) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26005879) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Critical Care Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005879 ) Department of Critical Care Medicine School of Medicine Faculty Position – BE/BC Critical Care Intensivist Description–External: The Department of Critical Care Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine and UPMC is seeking board-eligible or board-certified intensivists to join our faculty in the Cardiothoracic Intensive Care Unit (CTICU) at UPMC Presbyterian. We welcome applications from clinicians, clinician-educators, and clinician-scientists who are committed to delivering high-quality multidisciplinary care, educating trainees, and contributing to the academic mission of the department. The successful candidate will provide attending-level critical care for a high-acuity cardiothoracic population, including patients after cardiac and thoracic surgery; patients with cardiogenic shock, respiratory failure, pulmonary hypertension, advanced heart failure, or complex arrhythmias; and patients requiring temporary or durable mechanical circulatory support, extracorporeal membrane oxygenation, ventricular assist devices, Impella support, or intra-aortic balloon pump therapy. The role requires clinical judgment, advanced hemodynamic management, effective communication, and the ability to work closely with cardiac surgery, thoracic surgery, cardiology, heart failure, transplant, perfusion, advanced practice providers, nursing, respiratory therapy, pharmacy, and other members of the multidisciplinary team. Primary responsibilities include providing clinical coverage in the CTICU at UPMC Presbyterian; leading multidisciplinary ICU rounds; developing and implementing evidence-based diagnostic and therapeutic plans; supervising and teaching fellows, residents, medical students, and advanced practice providers; maintaining timely and accurate documentation; participating in quality improvement, patient safety, and operational initiatives; and supporting an inclusive learning and clinical environment. Faculty may also have opportunities to provide clinical care in other ICUs across the UPMC Health System based on departmental needs, clinical expertise, and mutual agreement. Minimum objective qualifications; other desirable qualifications: Applicants must hold an MD or DO degree, be board-certified or board-eligible in critical care medicine by a United States accreditation board and be eligible for medical licensure in Pennsylvania. Base training may include internal medicine, emergency medicine, surgery, anesthesiology, neurology, or another relevant discipline with accredited critical care training. Required qualifications include excellent communication skills, professionalism, sound clinical judgment, and a commitment to teamwork, education, patient-centered care, and a respectful and inclusive academic environment. Prior clinical experience or focused training in cardiothoracic critical care, ECMO, mechanical circulatory support, advanced hemodynamic management, perioperative cardiothoracic care, echocardiography, quality improvement, education, or clinical research is desirable but not required. About the Department: The Department of Critical Care Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine is the nation’s first and one of the foremost stand-alone academic departments devoted to critical care medicine. In partnership with UPMC, department faculty provide state-of-the-art multidisciplinary care for critically ill adult and pediatric patients across the UPMC Health System. The department is also a national leader in critical care education, faculty development, quality improvement, and research, with programs that span clinical care, translational science, population health, implementation science, and health services research. Rank and/or title; salary range or minimum: Academic appointment will be at the rank of Professor in the non-tenure stream, commensurate with qualifications, experience, and academic accomplishments. Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, list of three references, and any required application materials through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center, position 26005879. Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh - join.pitt.edu. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006117&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26006117) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26006117) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Pharm-Pharmacy & Therapeutics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006117 ) University of Pittsburgh Tenure-Track Assistant/Associate Professor/Professor Outcomes Research Department of Pharmacy & Therapeutics School of Pharmacy The Department of Pharmacy & Therapeutics of the University of Pittsburgh School of Pharmacy is seeking a highly motivated individual for a tenure-track faculty position at the assistant professor, associate professor, or professor rank. The ideal candidate will have research experience in one or more of the following areas: outcomes research; population health; pharmacoepidemiology; health economics; health outcomes; data science; and predictive analytics. Priority will be given to candidates with a proven track record of competitive extramural funding. Candidates must have a PhD, MD, PharmD, or equivalent with postdoctoral training experience with a degree in public health, healthcare outcomes, pharmaceutical sciences, biomedical sciences, or a related field. Expertise in artificial intelligence is also desirable. This is an in person, on campus position. The University of Pittsburgh is in the top 2% of universities worldwide and is ranked # 7 in NIH funding with $1.5 Billion invested in research. The University was recently recognized by Forbes as a “New Ivy”—1 of only 10 public universities in the U.S with such a distinction. The School of Pharmacy was recently ranked # 8 by the US News and World Report . Job Description: Position Title: Assistant Professor / Associate Professor / Professor Essential Functions: · Serve as a research scholar, developing an independent, competitively funded research program focused or allied with drug or medication-related outcomes research, data analytics, or other focus area as outlined above. · Duties associated with the research and scholarship role include: Develop a successful track record of scholarship, which includes peer-reviewed publications and competitive grantsmanship related to the areas listed above. Provide research mentorship to students, fellows, and other trainees. · Serve as a faculty member who teaches or mentors graduate and professional students in the School of Pharmacy. · Serve as Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the Department of Pharmacy & Therapeutics through the following, additional duties, as assigned by the Department Chair: Participation in School committees (strategic planning, search committees, graduate committees) Representation of the program on department-, school-, and university-level committees and in community service activities Active participation in local, regional, and national professional organizations Other duties/tasks as assigned by the Department Chair. Qualifications and Experience: · Required: § A doctoral degree from an accredited university in pharmacy, medicine, public health, healthcare outcomes, engineering, or a related field. § Expertise drug or medication-related research. § An established track record of peer-reviewed publications and competitive grantsmanship Preferred: § Experience in teaching in professional and/or graduate programs § Priority will be given to candidates with a proven track record of competitive extramural funding. § Proficiency with artificial intelligence in research will also be viewed as valuable expertise. Rank is commensurate with academic experience and credentials, with the following as a general guide: Candidates at the Assistant Professor level should have experience in clinical, transitional, or basic science research. Candidates at the Associate Professor level should have 6 or more years of experience in research and be able to demonstrate evidence of a significant record of substantial clinical, translational, or basic science research. Candidate at the Professor level should have 10  or more years of experience in research and be able to demonstrate an excellent national reputation, along with evidence of a significant record of substantial clinical, translational, or basic science research. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Interested candidates should apply through Talent Center, ID 26006117 at https://www.join.pitt.edu/ The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Teaching Statement, Teaching Evaluations Optional Attachments : Research Statement Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005723&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty - Human Engineering Research Laboratories",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty - Human Engineering Research Laboratories (26005723) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty - Human Engineering Research Laboratories (26005723) Job Description Faculty - Human Engineering Research Laboratories Med-Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005723 ) The Department of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation is currently accepting applications for full-time doctoral-level faculty researchers to work within the Human Engineering Research Laboratories (HERL) at the rank of Assistant Professor, non-tenure stream. A PhD, MD, DO, or equivalent degree in Engineering, Sciences or Medicine is required. Compensation package will be commensurate with experience and accomplishment. Responsibilities will include: · Secure peer-reviewed funding and collaborate in the conduct of research and development. · Create, design, and participate in research protocols, data collection and analysis. · Dissemination of research and development through peer-reviewed publications and presentations. · Advise and mentor students and post-docs who are working on research and development projects. · Serve on HERL and other committees as approved by the HERL Director. · Engage in scholarly activity and participate as part of an interdisciplinary team to conduct and support an externally funded peer-reviewed research and development program. · Participate in professional development activities and demonstrate leadership or leadership potential within profession. · Represent HERL through service on university-level committees and in the broader community. Qualifications: Candidates should have skills to be an effective faculty member. Should be an effective mentor and leader with strong interpersonal, written, oral communication skills and the ability to interact effectively with all stakeholder groups, including students, research participants, faculty, staff, and administration, as well as professional, governmental, and community partners. The ideal candidate will: · Possess PhD in Rehabilitation Science, Engineering, Computer Science or a closely related field. · Possess a minimum of five years of relevant teaching/mentoring, participatory research & development, and/or administrative experience in rehabilitation, assistive technology or closely related field research. · Involvement in rehabilitation science, rehabilitation engineering, and/or assistive technology related organizations. · Possess organizational and teaching/mentoring skills and the ability to be a highly effective mentor to students, post-docs, and interns, and to work collaboratively in teams including faculty/staff. Interested candidates should apply to Requisition #26005723 at https://www.join.pitt.edu/ . The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006043&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006043) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006043) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Ophthalmology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006043 ) University of Pittsburgh, Ophthalmology Department is searching for an Assistant Professor, tenure-stream position. Focusing on the temporospatial production of retinal bipolar-cell subtypes.  We expect the position to develop a world-class research program, mentor postdoctoral fellows and graduate students, submit grants, prepare manuscripts and publications, make research presentations, and participate in the activities of the local, national, and international neuroscience and ophthalmology communities. Minimum experience:   MD and PhD in Biomedical Sciences Please apply through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center using this link Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh.  Under Requisition #: 26006043 The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
