    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006228&lang=en": {
      "title": "Medical-Surgical Nursing Faculty - Full-Time Non Tenure Stream",
      "description": "Job Description - Medical-Surgical Nursing Faculty - Full-Time Non Tenure Stream (26006228) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Medical-Surgical Nursing Faculty - Full-Time Non Tenure Stream (26006228) Job Description Medical-Surgical Nursing Faculty - Full-Time Non Tenure Stream Nurs-Acute and Tertiary Care - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006228 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing is seeking qualified applicants for full-time, non-tenure stream, Medical-Surgical faculty in the Department of Acute and Tertiary Care. This Appointment-Stream position will be a full-time faculty member in the Acute and Tertiary Care Department in the School of Nursing, who will be responsible for teaching, clinical instruction, scholarship, and service. Responsibilities will include teaching and mentoring students in both the classroom and clinical setting, contributing to course development and delivery, and supporting student learning, professional development, and readiness for practice. Expectations also include active and sustained engagement in scholarship, clinical innovation, and dissemination through publications and presentations. The faculty member will also participate in service activities that support the School, University, profession, and community, contributing to committees, professional organizations, clinical partnerships, and community-based initiatives in alignment with the mission of the institution. Other duties may be assigned based on department needs. Faculty members receive dedicated time and resources to ensure they can successfully conduct their program of research, disseminate their research, and develop professionally. Faculty promotion opportunities are available for all ranks. Faculty Requirements in the Appointment Stream (Non-Tenure Stream): Assistant Professor – A) An earned doctorate in nursing or a field related to the area of scholarship within the School of Nursing is required. B) Evidence of or potential for a sustained and impactful program of scholarship. C) Evidence of or potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring, and contributing to a learning environment that values evidence-based practice. Associate Professor – A) An earned doctorate in nursing or a field related to the area of scholarship within the School of Nursing is required. B) Evidence of a sustained and impactful program of scholarship that is nationally recognized. C) Evidence of excellence in teaching and mentoring, and contributing to a learning environment that values evidence-based practice. D) Evidence of or potential for leadership in the field. Professor – A) An earned doctorate in nursing or a field related to the area of scholarship within the School of Nursing is required. B) Evidence of a sustained and impactful program of scholarship that is internationally recognized. C) Evidence of excellence in teaching and mentoring, and contributing to a learning environment that values evidence-based practice. D) Evidence of leadership in the field. About the University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing: Since its founding in 1939, the University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing has provided faculty and students with the resources and support to generate new healthcare knowledge and the educational foundation to conduct evidence-based practice, engage in scholarly activities, and translate knowledge to improve the delivery of healthcare in Pennsylvania, the nation, and throughout the world. As one of the nation's elite schools of nursing, Pitt Nursing receives millions of dollars in NIH grant funding each year, and U.S. News & World Report highly ranks multiple academic programs. A complete list of rankings for the School of Nursing can be found at: www.nursing.pitt.edu/about/our-rankings. About the University of Pittsburgh: Named a \"New Ivy\" by Forbes, the University of Pittsburgh is internationally recognized as a center of learning, innovation, and research. Pitt shares a campus with the world-class healthcare enterprise, UPMC. Collaboration between Pitt and UPMC results in an environment of interdisciplinary research and education, cutting-edge evidence-based practice, and an infrastructure that fosters career development and sustained successes. Apply Now: Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Candidates should apply online at https://www.join.pitt.edu/ and search for requisition number: 26006228. For more information on the School of Nursing, visit www.nursing.pitt.edu. As part of your application, please provide a statement of your area of scholarship and why you believe you will be successful at Pitt Nursing. Reasons to work at Pitt: The University offers exceptional benefits that include education benefits, health and wellness benefits, and a generous retirement plan. There are also generous tuition and educational benefits. Information about these and other benefits can be found on the University's HR website: Benefits | Human Resources | University of Pittsburgh As part of your application, please provide a statement of your area of scholarship, and why you believe you will be successful at Pitt Nursing. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Optional Attachments : Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005746&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time (26005746) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time (26005746) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time Med-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005746 ) Faculty Positions in Space and Global Biomedicine Assistant Professor or Associate Professor, Tenure Stream Trivedi Institute for Space and Global Biomedicine University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine The University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine's Trivedi Institute for Space and Global Biomedicine invites applications for full-time faculty positions at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level in the tenure stream. The Trivedi Institute is an interdisciplinary research institute bringing together space science, engineering, biology, and medicine to advance biomedical discovery and innovation. The Institute uses spaceflight and space-relevant environments as platforms for understanding biology, developing new medical technologies, and translating discoveries into solutions that benefit human health on Earth and beyond. The Institute's mission spans fundamental discovery, translational innovation, and the development of approaches relevant to human health and resilience in space, terrestrial, and resource-constrained environments. We seek outstanding faculty whose research will contribute to this interdisciplinary mission. Areas of interest include cell and molecular biology, human physiology, biomedical technologies, computational and systems approaches, biomanufacturing, sustainable biological systems, and related areas of biomedical science and engineering. Candidates whose research crosses traditional disciplinary boundaries and creates connections between fundamental biological discovery and translational applications are particularly encouraged to apply. These areas reflect the Institute's publicly articulated research pillars while allowing candidates to bring forward their own scientific programs. Successful candidates will be expected to develop and maintain an innovative, externally funded research program; publish impactful scholarship; collaborate with investigators across disciplines; contribute to the scientific programs and intellectual community of the Trivedi Institute; and participate in the education and mentorship of students and trainees. The anticipated distribution of effort is approximately 80% research, 10% teaching, 9% administrative activities , and 1% service activities. Applicants should hold a PhD in a relevant field, including biological or biomedical sciences, life sciences, engineering or bioengineering, computational sciences, and related disciplines; an MD; or an equivalent doctoral degree and have appropriate postgraduate research training. Candidates at the Assistant Professor level should have 1-5 years of experience, demonstrate strong potential to develop an independent research program, obtain external research funding, and establish a record of impactful scholarship. Candidates at the Associate Professor level should have 6-10 years of experience and have an established record of independent research, peer-reviewed scholarship, and external research funding. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The successful candidate's primary academic appointment will be made in an appropriate department within the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine based on the candidate's scientific background, qualifications, and research interests. The position will be based at the Trivedi Institute for Space and Global Biomedicine, 450 Technology Drive, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter, research statement describing current and future research directions, and [names and contact information for three references / three letters of recommendation]. Applications will be reviewed beginning October 15 and will continue until the position is filled. Qualified applicants should apply through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center at join.pitt.edu, requisition # 26005746. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005967&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Professor - Full-Time (26005967) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Professor - Full-Time (26005967) Job Description Faculty Professor - Full-Time Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005967 ) Qualified applicants seeking opportunities in clinical programs may find recruitment in The Department of Pediatrics of the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine Pediatric subspecialty programs: Our Subspecialties include: • Adolescent Medicine • Allergy • Bone Marrow Transplantation • Cardiology • Child Advocacy • Child Development • Hospitalists • Emergency Medicine • Endocrinology • Gastroenterology • General Academic Pediatrics • Hematology/Oncology • Infectious Diseases • Newborn Medicine • Neurology • Palliative Care and Supportive Medicine • Pulmonology • Rheumatology Job Description and Qualifications The position is for the recruitment of an Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the appointment (non-tenure) stream. Available positions are open to all applicants who hold a doctoral-level degree Education in the field of medicine (MD, DO), are board certified or board eligible, are qualified for medical licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, and meet the minimum position credentials for the pediatric specialty to provide clinical service. Responsibilities will include patient care, teaching, and research as determined by the chairman and the associated division chief. Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Professor positions in the appointment stream at the University of Pittsburgh, with rank and salary commensurate with experience and academic credentials. General rank requirements: Assistant Professors have 1-6 years of experience with demonstrated academic progress/contributions in their pediatric specialty; Associate Professors have 7-10 years of experience with significant demonstrated academic progress/contributions in their pediatric specialty; Professors have 10 or more years of experience with a clear demonstration of leadership, academic excellence and innovation in their pediatric specialty. Not all divisions have active recruitments; however, interested candidates can inquire about potential opportunities available in the Department of Pediatrics by applying to requisition number # 26005967 on Pitt Talent Center by visiting https://www.join.pitt.edu/ The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. See appended Job Posting The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004728&lang=en": {
      "title": "Professor of Endodontics - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Professor of Endodontics - Full-Time (26004728) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Professor of Endodontics - Full-Time (26004728) Job Description Professor of Endodontics - Full-Time Dent Med-Endodontics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004728 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Dental Medicine invites applications for the position of Chair of the Department of Endodontics. This is an open-rank, full-time appointment stream (nontenure) faculty position. The academic rank will be determined as commensurate with the candidate's qualifications and experience. The Chair will have a unique opportunity to lead a vibrant, nationally recognized department with a longstanding tradition of excellence in education, clinical care, research, and service. Supported by a thriving clinical enterprise, the department is well positioned for continued growth and innovation. The successful candidate will build on these strengths to shape the department's future, expand its impact, and foster excellence across its academic, clinical, and research missions. A key expectation of the role is to recruit, develop, and retain outstanding faculty while attracting highly talented residents who will contribute to the department's continued national prominence. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, residents, and institutional leaders, the Chair will advance initiatives that promote oral health equity, strengthen community-based education, expand access to care in rural and underserved communities, enhance translational and population health research, and further elevate evidence-based clinical practice. Key responsibilities include: provide visionary leadership aligned with the school's mission to improve oral and overall health through education, research, and service; didactic and clinical instruction of residents, scholarly activities, and service; provide support to the program director of the Advanced Dental Education and Residency Program in Endodontics; engage in scholarship; mentor faculty in teaching and in securing extramural research funding; advance curricular integration of endodontics in predoctoral and residency programs; and manage departmental resources, personnel, and strategic planning with transparency and fiscal accountability. Additional departmental administrative duties may also apply. Participation in the University Dental Health Services faculty practice is also available. Qualified applicants must hold a dental degree and an advanced education certificate in Endodontics from a CODA-accredited program. The applicant must be a Diplomate of the American Board of Endodontics (ABE) and be able to obtain and maintain a Pennsylvania dental license. The applicant should have a minimum of five years of clinical practice and a minimum of five years of teaching experience as a full-time or part-time faculty member associated with an endodontic department. Preference will be given to those with additional academic and/or leadership training, a documented record of achievement in teaching, scholarship, and service related to the specialty of endodontics; and demonstrated leadership experience and success in fostering collaborative, interdisciplinary teams. The University of Pittsburgh is a top-ranked public research institution and is currently ranked 7th among U.S. universities in NIH funding. The School of Dental Medicine is ranked 7th in FY25 in NIDCR funding among U.S. dental schools. The school is located on the University's main campus in Pittsburgh, contiguous with the other five health science schools. UPMC is an internationally renowned academic medical center and health care enterprise with a robust infrastructure to support clinicians with innovative clinical programs and biomedical and health sciences research, making discoveries that save lives and change the landscape of patient care. As part of the clinical practice and faculty of the University of Pittsburgh, the practitioner will have the opportunity to collaborate with clinicians, innovators, and investigators from around the world and become part of a vibrant community of health care providers dedicated to making a difference in their chosen field and in the lives of others. To apply, please go to join.pitt.edu, select Faculty Positions, and search for keyword 26004728. Please upload a curriculum vitae, the names and contact information for three references, and a cover letter that describes your interest in the position, qualifications, and experience; outlines your vision for the future of the department; and explains why you want to join the Pitt Dental Medicine team. The search committee will begin reviewing applications upon receipt. Only applicants who appear best qualified will be invited to a personal interview. If the intended academic rank is Assistant Professor, the candidate must provide at least three letters of recommendation. These letters may be uploaded with your application or submitted via email. If the intended academic rank is either Associate Professor or Professor, please upload a contact list of six external referees whom we may contact on your behalf for an appointment review. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation, Teaching Statement, Teaching Evaluations Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006075&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Clinical Assistant - Part-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Clinical Assistant - Part-Time (26006075) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Clinical Assistant - Part-Time (26006075) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Clinical Assistant - Part-Time Dent Med-Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006075 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Dental Medicine is accepting applications for a part-time, appointment stream faculty position at the academic rank of Clinical Assistant Professor in the Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery at the commitment effort of one day per week. The faculty rank and salary will depend on experience and qualifications. The primary responsibility of this position would be: - Provide clinic coverage for pre-doctoral/resident students in Oral Maxillofacial Surgery - Teaching and clinic assignments will be at the chair’s discretion Applicants must have a DDS / DMD degree from an accredited school and a dental license to practice in the State of Pennsylvania. We are seeking candidates with significant clinical experience as an oral and maxillofacial surgeon and have graduated from an Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery residency program and must be board certified. The school is located on the University's main campus in Pittsburgh, contiguous with the other five health science schools. The School of Dental Medicine works as a key collaborative partner with the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC), an internationally renowned academic medical center and healthcare enterprise. The robust infrastructure supports clinicians and educators with innovative clinical programs, biomedical research, and health sciences research, enabling discoveries that save lives and change the landscape of patient care. As part of the clinical practice and faculty of the University of Pittsburgh, the practitioner will have the opportunity to collaborate with clinicians, innovators, and investigators from around the world and become part of a vibrant community of healthcare providers dedicated to making a difference in their chosen field and in the lives of others. To apply, please go to join.pitt.edu, select faculty positions, and search 26006075 in the keyword search. Please upload a curriculum vitae, and a statement describing your interest in the position, qualifications, and experience. The search committee will begin reviewing applications upon receipt.  Only applicants who appear best qualified will be invited for a personal interview. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005977&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Visiting Research Assistant",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Visiting Research Assistant (26005977) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Visiting Research Assistant (26005977) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Visiting Research Assistant Chemistry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005977 ) The Department of Chemistry at the University of Pittsburgh invites applications for a full-time Visiting Research Assistant Professor to lead and conduct research on the chirality-induced spin selectivity (CISS) effect. The successful candidate will work closely with Professor Haitao Liu and his research group to investigate how molecular chirality governs spin-dependent electron transport and reactivity at surfaces and interfaces, with applications spanning spintronics, enantioselective electrochemistry and catalysis, and spin-controlled processes in molecular and biomolecular systems. Primary Responsibilities Design, execute, and interpret experiments probing spin-polarized charge transport through chiral molecules, self-assembled monolayers, and chiral thin films. Develop and apply surface- and interface-sensitive measurements relevant to CISS, which may include magnetoresistance and spin-dependent transport measurements, electrochemical methods (cyclic voltammetry, EIS, chronoamperometry), spin-polarized or magnetic-field-modulated electrochemistry, and characterization by AFM, XPS, QCM/QCM-D, ellipsometry, and related techniques. Prepare and characterize chiral molecular assemblies and substrates, including DNA-based and other biomolecular chiral systems where relevant. Author peer-reviewed publications and contribute to conference presentations and dissemination of results. Contribute to the preparation of grant proposals and reports to federal agencies and other sponsors. Mentor and train graduate and undergraduate researchers, and help maintain shared instrumentation and safe laboratory practices. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Chemistry, Physics, Materials Science, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research experience relevant to CISS, spin-dependent phenomena, electrochemistry, surface science, or molecular electronics, evidenced by a strong publication record. Hands-on expertise with one or more relevant experimental platforms (e.g., electrochemistry, surface characterization, magnetotransport, or spin-sensitive measurements). Ability to work independently, design rigorous experiments, and communicate results effectively in writing and in presentations. Preferred Qualifications Direct experience measuring or modeling the CISS effect or spin-polarized transport in molecular and solid state systems. Familiarity with chiral self-assembled monolayers, DNA nanostructures, or chiral inorganic/hybrid materials. Experience with instrument development, automation, or custom measurement setups. A record of successful collaboration across chemistry, physics, and materials science. Contributions to grant writing and evidence of emerging research independence. Appointment Terms This is a full-time, visiting research assistant professor appointment, the initial appointment term will be 1 year, with renewal contingent on performance and the availability of funding. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of research interests and experience (2–3 pages), and the names and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation Optional Attachments : Research Statement Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005875&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26005875) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26005875) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Pathology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005875 ) The Department of Pathology is recruiting an Assistant professor (5 years’ experience), Associate Professor (6-10 years of experience) or Professor (10+ years of experience) appointment stream, faculty position for the Division of Liver, Kidney, Cardiac, Small Bowel, and Transplantation Pathology. Experience in a large hospital-based native and allograft liver and kidney pathology service is desirable. The successful candidate will contribute to varied divisional diagnostic, research, and educational activities. The position will be responsible for reporting on allograft and native liver, heart, small bowel, and kidney biopsies. Academic development will focus on scientific areas related to clinical interests and responsibilities. The division is fully equipped to study spatial and general tissue proteogenomic profiling, multiplex labeling, image analysis, and practical AI applications related to clinical responsibilities. Interest in these areas is an advantage; unique opportunities exist to participate in multicenter study tissue analyses using the above approaches. Qualifications: Candidates must possess: · M.D degree · Board certification in Anatomic Pathology · Eligibility for Pennsylvania medical licensure is required Preferred qualifications include: · Fellowship training in a relevant pathology subspecialty Salary and benefits: · Salary will commensurate with experience · Full-time faculty member at the University of Pittsburgh as well as a participant in the UPMC/UPP faculty practice plan Please include (1) curriculum vitae; (2) a letter of interest describing research and academic interests, as well as (3) a brief statement of personal goals. For questions, please contact demetrisaj@upmc.edu or by mail at: Anthony J. Demetris, MD Director, Division of Liver, Kidney, and Transplantation Pathology UPMC Montefiore, Room E741 3459 Fifth Avenue Pittsburgh, PA 15213 To apply: Go to TALENT CENTER at www.join.pitt.edu and search for requisition 26005875 in the keyword. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004389&lang=en": {
      "title": "PROFESSOR OF LEGAL WRITING - School of Law",
      "description": "Job Description - PROFESSOR OF LEGAL WRITING - School of Law (26004389) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - PROFESSOR OF LEGAL WRITING - School of Law (26004389) Job Description PROFESSOR OF LEGAL WRITING - School of Law Law-Faculty - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004389 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Law invites applications for one or more full-time faculty positions at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Legal Writing. The position is part of a system of contracts progressing to presumptively renewable long-term contracts, separate from the University’s tenure stream. Pitt Law’s legal writing program develops the legal analytical skills of students and equips them to write and speak clearly and persuasively, in a manner appropriate for different audiences and purposes in law practice. The first-year Legal Analysis & Writing course spans two semesters, typically including “objective” writing assignments in the fall and persuasive writing assignments and oral argument in the spring. The course typically also encompasses related skill sets, including client interviewing and negotiation, among others. While the course covers the basics of legal research and includes open-resource assignments, students are separately required to take a one-credit course on the fundamentals of legal research, taught by library faculty, in the spring semester of their first year. Legal Writing faculty members typically teach two small sections of first-year Legal Analysis and Writing in the fall and spring (approximately 15-20 students per section), for a total of four credits for each section. They may also teach upper-level writing courses and may have some administrative duties. Legal Writing faculty have the opportunity to shape the future direction of the Legal Writing program and the law school more broadly as a full participant in faculty governance at Pitt Law. Minimum Requirements: J.D. from an ABA-accredited law school, excellent writing skills, and an outstanding academic record. Experience teaching legal writing and law practice experience are preferred. Candidates should be able to work effectively with a wide variety of students and have an interest in developing legal writing experiences for law students within a community that supports collaboration and innovative teaching. Candidates are encouraged to present their own ideas about teaching legal writing in an era of profound change and uncertainty in the legal profession and legal education, brought on by generative AI. Please provide a list of at least three (3) references with full contact information. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006096&lang=en": {
      "title": "Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist",
      "description": "Job Description - Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist (26006096) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist (26006096) Job Description Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist Falk School - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006096 ) Elementary School (K-8) Learning Specialist Falk Laboratory School, a coeducational K-8 school at the University of Pittsburgh, seeks a full-time educator to work with children who have a range of learning differences. This role begins January 2027 . Candidates must have empathy for, and a genuine interest in, developing positive educational experiences for students with learning differences. Among the professional duties of a Falk Learning Specialist are the following: Collaborate with staff members and families to create and implement intervention programs that maximize students’ access to the general education content Administer initial screening and diagnostic testing in both reading and mathematics to identify students who could benefit from remedial instruction Develop and teach motivating, engaging lessons that are grounded in best practices, and are appropriate to students’ ages, grade levels, and abilities Apply and support accommodations to support instruction Observe, evaluate, and prepare reports on students’ progress A Master of Education Degree in the field of special education or a related field is required. Broad experience in a school setting is advantageous as the position involves partnering across disciplines and grade levels. The minimum base salary is $50,000 (10-month contract); credit will be given for years of relevant experience. Falk Laboratory School, a department in the School of Education at the University of Pittsburgh, offers excellent benefits. Materials should be uploaded electronically to: https://www.join.pitt.edu/ . Please submit: 1.     Letter of application 2.     A resume 3.     An educational philosophy that includes a vision for an ideal experience for students with learning differences 4.     Three letters of recommendation 5.     Official transcripts 6.     PA instructional certificate or equivalent, if applicable Questions about the position can be sent to Dr. Joanna Newlin, jmn56@pitt.edu , Director of Student Services or Dr. Molly Hicks, Director of Administrative Operations, meh479@pitt.edu . Review of applications will begin mid-October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Offer of employment is contingent on the candidate satisfactorily obtaining and passing the following prior to commencement of appointment: Pennsylvania Department of Human Services Child Abuse History Clearance, Pennsylvania State Police Criminal Record Check and FBI Criminal Record Check. Also, as required by Act 168 of 2014, candidate must satisfy the requirements stated on the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania Department of Education Sexual Misconduct/Abuse Disclosure Release Form. Proof of negative TB test required upon hire. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation, Teaching Statement, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005704&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005704) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005704) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005704 ) The Division of Rheumatology in the Department of Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh and UPMC are seeking an outstanding physician scientist at the Assistant Professor level (non-tenure track).  Physicians will be responsible for the management of patients with primary focus of working with dedicated scleroderma and Sjogren’s disease clinics, and corresponding observational cohort studies and clinical trials.   The physician will be responsible for both inpatient and outpatient cohorts of patients, will round at UPMC hospitals as assigned, and maintain at least six outpatient clinics per week and the continued care of those patients.  The physician will serve as a preceptor to fellows and residents and be involved in teaching at UPMC for trainees.  Physician will be 80% clinical, 10% research and 10% teaching. General rank requirements:  An Assistant Professor should have demonstrated teaching ability, experience in advanced study and research, or professional experience of a kind that would enable them to make an academic contribution.  The Assistant Professor should possess a doctoral or appropriate professional degree (MD or DO) and be Board Certified/Board Eligible.  They should exhibit promise of originality and excellence in some field of scholarship and should have demonstrated ability in guiding and counseling students.  To be appointed or promoted to an assistant professorship, a person should have the potential for promotion to Associate Professor. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae for position #26005704 and apply using this link: http://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004568&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26004568) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26004568) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004568 ) The Department of Medicine and Section of Palliative Care in the Division of General Internal Medicine is seeking a full-time physician (MD/DO), PhD scientist or PharmD in a relevant field with a research focus on palliative care and serious illness at the levels of Assistant Professor, appointment or tenure stream, Associate Professor, appointment or tenure stream and Professor, appointment stream or tenured depending on qualifications and career track to serve as the Associate Chief of Research (ACR) and Director of the Palliative Research Center (PaRC). In this role, the ACR will collaborate closely with the Section Faculty and report directly to the Section Chief. The Section of Palliative Care is a multidisciplinary team committed to improving quality of life for patients and families through delivery of quality palliative care, education of palliative care skills and advancement in palliative care innovation. We work with patients at academic hospitals and at outpatient clinics throughout the region. Our fellowship program is nationally recognized and comprised of four fellowship tracks to accommodate diverse career goals. The Palliative Research Center (PaRC) consists of faculty from across the Schools of Health Sciences, including researchers from palliative care and many medical subdisciplines, nursing, and public health. PaRC supports researchers throughout their careers and encourages collaboration between faculty members across disciplines. Key Responsibilities: Research Leadership – Develop and implement the strategic research mission of the Section and the Palliative Research Center (PaRC). Recruitment and Mentorship – Recruit junior and mid-level investigators and provide mentorship for palliative care investigators. Collaboration and Engagement – Promote synergy and partnerships across disciplines and University departments, schools and institutes. Grant Funding – Nurture collaborative relationships with foundations and industries and advance federal research projects (NIH, PCORI). Resources available: Palliative Research Center (PaRC) Center for Research on Health Care (CRHC) VA Center for Health Care Evaluation, Research Promotion (CHERP) Institute for Clinical Research Education (ICRE) Applicants for Assistant Professor, appointment or tenure stream, should have three or more years of experience in the field of clinical and/or health services research; have achieved or established the ability to attain external research funding; have dispersed results through peer-reviewed publications and other scientific forums; have noteworthy teaching experience; and established the capability for continued career development, promotion, and tenure. Applicants for Associate Professor, appointment or tenure stream, should have five or more years of experience in the field of clinical and/or health services research; have independent, external research funding and an extensive record of peer-reviewed publications; have substantial teaching experience; and demonstrate the ability for continued, impactful, independent scholarly contributions and leadership. Applicants for Professor, appointment stream or tenured, will have served five to seven years as Associate Professor. The rank of professor regards the individual accomplishments of respected knowledge and status in a distinguished ﬁeld of learning and the achievement of successful teaching knowledge and practices. The professor should have obtained enhanced stature in their ﬁeld through contributions of scholarship, professional practice, and leadership in professional and learning organizations. We offer a competitive salary, comprehensive benefits package, and a dynamic working environment. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae and apply to requisition number 26004568 via: https://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer/disability/veteran. About UPMC: The University of Pittsburgh and its partner, the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC), are committed to excellence in biomedical science and health care in southwestern Pennsylvania.  Together, they focus on training the next generation of health care specialists, conducting groundbreaking research, and delivering outstanding patient care.  The University encompasses six schools of health sciences, all sharing a mission to advance education, biomedical research, and health promotion.  Notably, the University has doubled its NIH support since 1998 and is a leader in NIH-funded institutions, underscoring its commitment to research infrastructure and faculty recruitment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26004567&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26004567) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26004567) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26004567 ) The Department of Medicine and Section of Palliative Care in the Division of General Internal Medicine is seeking a full-time physician (MD/DO) in a relevant field with a research focus on palliative care and serious illness at the levels of Assistant Professor, appointment or tenure stream, Associate Professor, appointment or tenure stream and Professor, appointment stream or tenured depending on qualifications and career track to serve as the Associate Chief of Research (ACR) and Director of the Palliative Research Center (PaRC). In this role, the ACR will collaborate closely with the Section Faculty and report directly to the Section Chief. The Section of Palliative Care is a multidisciplinary team committed to improving quality of life for patients and families through delivery of quality palliative care, education of palliative care skills and advancement in palliative care innovation. We work with patients at academic hospitals and at outpatient clinics throughout the region. Our fellowship program is nationally recognized and comprised of four fellowship tracks to accommodate diverse career goals. The Palliative Research Center (PaRC) consists of faculty from across the Schools of Health Sciences, including researchers from palliative care and many medical subdisciplines, nursing, and public health. PaRC supports researchers throughout their careers and encourages collaboration between faculty members across disciplines. Key Responsibilities: Research Leadership – Develop and implement the strategic research mission of the Section and the Palliative Research Center (PaRC). Recruitment and Mentorship – Recruit junior and mid-level investigators and provide mentorship for palliative care investigators. Collaboration and Engagement – Promote synergy and partnerships across disciplines and University departments, schools and institutes. Grant Funding – Nurture collaborative relationships with foundations and industries and advance federal research projects (NIH, PCORI). Resources Available: Palliative Research Center (PaRC) Center for Research on Health Care (CRHC) VA Center for Health Care Evaluation, Research Promotion (CHERP) Institute for Clinical Research Education (ICRE) Applicants for Assistant Professor, appointment or tenure stream, should have three or more years of experience in the field of clinical and/or health services research; have achieved or established the ability to attain external research funding; have dispersed results through peer-reviewed publications and other scientific forums; have noteworthy teaching experience; and established the capability for continued career development, promotion, and tenure. Applicants for Associate Professor, appointment or tenure stream, should have five or more years of experience in the field of clinical and/or health services research; have independent, external research funding and an extensive record of peer-reviewed publications; have substantial teaching experience; and demonstrate the ability for continued, impactful, independent scholarly contributions and leadership. Applicants for Professor, appointment stream or tenured, will have served five to seven years as Associate Professor. The rank of professor regards the individual accomplishments of respected knowledge and status in a distinguished ﬁeld of learning and the achievement of successful teaching knowledge and practices. The professor should have obtained enhanced stature in their ﬁeld through contributions of scholarship, professional practice, and leadership in professional and learning organizations. We offer a competitive salary, comprehensive benefits package, and a dynamic working environment. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae and apply to requisition number 26004567 via: https://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer/disability/veteran. About UPMC: The University of Pittsburgh and its partner, the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC), are committed to excellence in biomedical science and health care in southwestern Pennsylvania.  Together, they focus on training the next generation of health care specialists, conducting groundbreaking research, and delivering outstanding patient care.  The University encompasses six schools of health sciences, all sharing a mission to advance education, biomedical research, and health promotion.  Notably, the University has doubled its NIH support since 1998 and is a leader in NIH-funded institutions, underscoring its commitment to research and infrastructure and faculty recruitment. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005747&lang=en": {
      "title": "Pittsburgh Hearing Research Center, Associate Professor/Professor - Tenure Stream",
      "description": "Job Description - Pittsburgh Hearing Research Center, Associate Professor/Professor - Tenure Stream (26005747) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Pittsburgh Hearing Research Center, Associate Professor/Professor - Tenure Stream (26005747) Job Description Pittsburgh Hearing Research Center, Associate Professor/Professor - Tenure Stream Med-Otolaryngology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005747 ) The Department of Otolaryngology and the Pittsburgh Hearing Research Center (PHRC) at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine are recruiting a leader in hearing research for a full-time, tenure-stream faculty position at the Associate Professor or Professor level. We welcome candidates who advance our mechanistic understanding of hearing, and/or who work on the understanding, diagnosis, or treatment of hearing loss and related disorders. Exceptional Assistant Professor candidates with a clearly emerging leadership profile will also be considered. Faculty rank will be based on qualifications and experience. The successful candidate will hold a PhD in any of the fields of neuroscience, molecular/cell biology/biochemistry, cognitive and neural systems, computational science, communication science, bioengineering, genetics, epidemiology, and data science. We are seeking an exceptional scientist with an established vigorous independent research program focused on hearing, hearing loss, or related disorders. We offer a very generous start-up package, plus the opportunity to help shape the newly established Pittsburgh Hearing Institute . The Institute brings basic scientists, clinician-scientists, and clinical care together in one location, co-locating neurotology, audiology, vestibular medicine, and basic/translational hearing research, so that research and patient care can directly inform one another rather than operate separately. Our hearing research community is further supported by certificate graduate programs and NIH-funded training grants ( https://phrc.pitt.edu/education-training ) dedicated to the training of the next generation of hearing and vestibular scientists in basic and translational research. The faculty position is within the vibrant and highly interactive basic, translational and clinical; neuroscience research community of the University of Pittsburgh, including the Department of Neurobiology ( https://www.neurobio.pitt.edu/ ), the UPMC Vision Institute ( http://www.upmc.com/services/eye ), the Center for Neuroscience at the University of Pittsburgh ( http://www.cnup.pitt.edu ), the Pittsburgh Institute for Neurodegenerative disorders ( http://www.pind.pitt.edu ) and the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center ( http://www.upmc.com/about/facts/pages/default.aspx ). Successful candidates will join an active auditory research community with diverse colleagues across the University of Pittsburgh and the adjacent Carnegie Mellon University whose research spans human clinical and behavioral research, auditory cognitive neuroscience, and systems, cellular and molecular neuroscience. Applicants should apply through the Talent Center at https://www.join.pitt.edu , using Requisition #26005747. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=25003903&lang=en": {
      "title": "Mid-Career Urologist Specialized in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS) / Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery (FPMRS)",
      "description": "Job Description - Mid-Career Urologist Specialized in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS) / Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery (FPMRS) (25003903) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Mid-Career Urologist Specialized in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS) / Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery (FPMRS) (25003903) Job Description Mid-Career Urologist Specialized in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS) / Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery (FPMRS) Med-Urology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 25003903 ) The Department of Urology at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine and the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC) is seeking a full-time faculty member. We are seeking a mid-career urologist specializing in Urologic Reconstructive and Pelvic Surgery (URPS) / Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery (FPMRS) to advance the care of women with complex urologic conditions. The candidate will lead the growth of a comprehensive program in female urology, integrating clinical care, research, and education, while mentoring trainees and junior faculty. This position carries a dual appointment with the Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences, with expectations to work collaboratively with the Division of Urogynecology to develop joint initiatives. Th e position will include an appointment in the Department of Urology at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine as an Associate Professor or Professor in the appointment stream.  Candidates at the Associate Professor level should have 6 - 9 years of experience, and at the Professor level, 10+ years of experience.  The candidate must have an M.D. in Urology with appropriate board certification/eligibility; experience in a large hospital service is beneficial.  Eligibility for medical licensure to practice in Pennsylvania is required. Qualified applicants should apply via Talent Center under Requisition Num ber: 25003903 The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005395&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005395) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005395) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Psychiatry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005395 ) Assistant Professor of Psychiatry University of Pittsburgh, Department of Psychiatry Pittsburgh, United States Job Description The Department of Psychiatry at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking researchers for full-time faculty positions investigating psychiatric illness. Positions are available at the assistant professor level within the appointment (non-tenure) stream. Growth is sought in both preclinical and clinical approaches towards understanding psychiatric illness. Consequently, multiple positions are available. Primary selection criteria are history of productivity and ability to enhance an interactive and dynamic mental health research community within and across departments in the greater Pittsburgh academic environment. Primarily, the search committee will look for: Success in authoring papers published in refereed journals. These may include original research and review articles. The quality of the journals themselves and the position of authorship will also be considered. Success in securing federal funding from the National Institutes of Health (NIH). However, success in obtaining funding from other sources (such as state and foundation funding) will also be considered. Presentations of research and/or scholarly material and published abstracts associated with professional or scientific meetings. Successful candidates will join a vibrant and highly interactive research community with a long history of excellence in basic, translational, and clinical research. The Department of Psychiatry is prepared to invest substantial resources to ensure success. Qualifications: PhD in Psychology, Neuroscience, Translational Science, or related field. Demonstrated research skills Strong organizational skills Flexibility and ability to work in a rapidly changing/growing educational institution Job Responsibilities: · Establish and sustain an independent, externally funded research program in psychiatric illness · Publish scholarly work in peer ‑ reviewed journals and present findings at professional meetings. · Collaborate with departmental and interdisciplinary research teams at Pitt and UPMC. · Contribute to the academic mission through teaching, mentoring, and service, as appropriate. About the Employer At the University of Pittsburgh Department of Psychiatry, we excel in our mission to: provide superb behavioral health services to our patients and their families; pursue the development of better diagnostic techniques and therapeutic interventions through innovative research; provide a stimulating learning environment for medical and graduate students, residents, psychology interns, and postdoctoral fellows. An essential partner in this work is UPMC Western Psychiatric Hospital, a national leader in innovative treatment of mental health and addiction disorders. Moreover, Pitt Psychiatry's preeminent academic faculty of more than 230 members trained in multiple basic and clinical science disciplines is at the heart of our success in providing superior behavioral health care and in training the next generation of innovative researchers and clinicians. Areas of Research Psychology Psychiatry Neuroscience How to Apply Please apply by going to our job site ( https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobsearch.ftl ), searching job code 26005395 in the keyword search, and submitting your materials through our Pitt system. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005482&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26005482) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26005482) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Pathology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005482 ) RANK/TITLE: Assistant Professor (1-5 years of experience) Associate Professor (6-10 years of experience) or Professor (10+ years of experience) appointment stream. DEPARTMENT/DIVISION: The Department of Pathology, Division of Anatomic Pathology of UPMC, University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC) and University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine (UPSOM) is recruiting for the Director of the Head and Neck Pathology Center of Excellence (COE). The position will be in the appointment stream academic clinical track. The candidate needs to have subspecialty training and academic interest in Head and Neck Surgical Pathology. The Head and Neck Pathology Center of Excellence (COE) consists of Four Head and Neck Pathologists and is known for its expertise in neoplastic and non-neoplastic Head and Neck diseases. This COE processes over 3,500 Head and Neck cases per year and serves as a local, regional and national consultation reference laboratory including telepathology. The Head and Neck Pathology COE has very close ties with the Head and Neck Surgical and Medical Oncology groups. The University of Pittsburgh Head and Neck Team has a very strong record of Federal and Industry funding and collaborations and has been consistently funded as a SPORE (Specialized Program Of Research Excellence) program, one of the highest research designation s and pragmatic funding by the NIH. · A secondary appointment in Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery will be provided. · The potential to engage with and support the multidisciplinary head and neck research team, including on programmatic grants, is expected. The Head and Neck COE offers a one-year ACGME accredited Head and Neck Pathology Fellowship program. This position is based at UPMC Presbyterian-Shadyside Hospitals, which primarily provides diagnostic support to the Hillman Cancer Center. The Dept. of Pathology at UPMC has a well-established Molecular, Digital and Computational Pathology infrastructure and resources. There is ongoing investment in Digital Pathology and AI applications in Pathology. Candidates would have extensive oversight and involvement in translational pathology utilizing the shared resources of our Imaging and Digital Pathology Laboratories, Molecular Anatomic Pathology and FISH laboratories. Individuals would be provided with guaranteed protected time. The successful candidate will be expected to provide leadership and guidance to develop and leverage diagnostic and research initiatives using available resources. JOB DUTIES: · As the Head and Neck COE Director, oversee the functioning of Head and Neck Pathology operations. · Work closely with the system Executive Vice-Chair for Anatomic Pathology. · Represent the Dept. at various COE specific meetings at UPMC/Hillman Cancer Center. · Represent the Dept. nationally and internationally. · Mentor faculty and provide oversight for the deliverance of the mission and goals of the Dept. · Teach Head and Neck Pathology fellows and Pathology residents. · Sign out of surgical pathology cases, as needed. · Participate in research initiatives, as needed. QUALIFICATIONS: · Must have an M.D./DO and Board certified in Anatomic Pathology with specialty training and academic interest in Head and Neck Pathology. · Eligibility for medical licensure in Pennsylvania is required. · A good record of and commitment to scholarly activities and publications. SALARY AND BENEFITS: Salary will be commensurate with experience. Full-time faculty member at the University of Pittsburgh as well as a participant in the UPMC/UPP faculty practice plan. APPLICATION: For questions please contact: Rajiv Dhir, MD, MBA Executive Vice Chair and Medical Director of Anatomic Pathology Services at UPMC Phone: (412) 623-1321 E-mail: dhirr@upmc.edu To Apply: Go to TALENT CENTER at www.join.pitt.edu and search for requisition number 26005482 in keyword. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005809&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time (26005809) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time (26005809) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005809 ) UPSOM Department of Medicine seeks an innovative, committed, and collaborative leader to serve as its inaugural Associate Dean for Assessment and Educational Evaluation. This is a pivotal moment in medical education, one defined by competency-based assessment, data-informed decision-making, and an unwavering commitment to continuous improvement. The Associate Dean will closely partner with the Assistant Dean for Accreditation and Continuous Quality Improvement (ACQI) in leading an office that spans assessment, evaluation (educational and non-educational), and ACQI. The Associate Dean will play a central role in shaping how UPSOM measures excellence, ensures accountability, and advances the quality and impact of its educational programs as it advances toward the goal of being recognized as one of the top 5 medical schools in the country. This position will be at the Associate Professor rank, appointment stream. Reporting to Abbas Hyderi, MD, MPH, Vice Dean for Education, the Associate Dean will design, implement, and oversee a comprehensive and integrated system of student assessment and educational program evaluation aligned with UPSOM’s mission, vision, and values. This leader will ensure that both learner performance and curricular effectiveness are systematically measured, thoughtfully analyzed, and continuously improved - building a culture where assessment is not episodic, but embedded, transparent, and mission-driven. In addition, the Associate Dean will lead efforts in curriculum mapping and integration to promote alignment of educational program objectives, course/clerkship objectives, and assessments. The role requires employing evidence-based approaches and contributing to national discussions on competency-based medical education, student assessment, educational program evaluation, and continuous improvement of medical education. The role will lead efforts in curriculum mapping and integration to enable the most effective alignment between instruction, learner assessment, and educational program evaluation. Primary Responsibilities: · Lead the design and implementation of a systematic program evaluation framework to monitor the effectiveness and quality of the curriculum and learning environment. · Analyze evaluation data and provide actionable recommendations for improvement to faculty, committees, and leadership. · Monitor evaluation outcomes, lead or guide associated quality improvement efforts as appropriate, and participate in the continuous quality improvement efforts. · Design, implement, and evaluate a comprehensive program of student assessment across the entirety of the curriculum, including working towards a competency-based medical approach. · Work with course and education program leaders to ensure a variety of robust student assessments (spanning medical knowledge, clinical skills, and workplace-based activities) that are aligned with UPSOM educational program objectives. · Work with course and education program leaders to ensure student assessments are aligned with accreditation expectations. Serve as content expert for LCME standards related to assessment. Prepare for and participate in accreditation reviews and site visits. Monitor and address any assessment or educational evaluation issues related to accreditation and regulatory compliance. · Monitor assessment outcomes, lead or guide associated continuous quality improvement efforts as appropriate and participate in the quality improvement efforts of the CQI Committee. · Create and oversee formative and summative assessment strategies, including performance-based assessments. · Employ evidence-based strategies and contribute to national discussions on competency-based medical education, student assessment, and continuous improvement of assessment initiatives. · Collaborate with information technology to streamline assessment and educational evaluation data collection, review, and monitoring including contributing to a nascent educational data warehouse. · Analyze and report data in a manner that effectively and clearly communicates student and program performance. · Lead data collection, processes, analyses, and reporting of student performance and post-graduation outcomes. · Prepare reports in support of accreditation and quality improvement processes. · Provide input into the Medical Student Performance Evaluation as needed. · Serve as a staff member on the Committee on Student Promotions to present select assessment information, answer questions, and provide context. · Oversee curriculum mapping to ensure alignment between educational program objectives, course/clerkship objectives, instructional methods, and assessment methods. · Collaborate with faculty and course leaders to identify gaps, redundancies, and opportunities for integration across the curriculum. · Ensure that curriculum maps are updated and maintained to support accreditation, student learning, and faculty development. · Work with the Curriculum Committee and related subcommittees to enhance horizontal and vertical integration of educational content and outcomes. · Provide direction and feedback to staff – support the hiring and onboarding of new staff. · Collaborate with school senior leadership to set and enforce overall assessment policies, procedures, and strategies. · Serve on internal and external committees related to role. · Disseminate experiences/scholarship in regional and national presentations and other activities to highlight the work done at UPSOM. · Build and maintain relationships with other medical schools, healthcare organizations, and community partners. · Serve as a member of the Vice Dean for Education leadership team. · Collaborate with and support the other assistant and associate deans with responsibilities in the medical education environment. Location: University of Pittsburgh is located in Pittsburgh, PA. Relocation to the Pittsburgh area is required for this role. Candidate Profile In terms of the performance and personal competencies required for the position, we would highlight the following: Education & Experience • A demonstrated leader in medical education (MD, PhD, EdD, or equivalent degree in a medical field) with an outstanding track record of accomplishment in medical education. • Five years of experience in undergraduate and/or graduate medical education with oversight of learner assessment and educational evaluation within a course, clerkship, or other curricular component. • 3-5 years of direct teaching experience of medical students, preferred. • Direct experience designing, implementing, and overseeing assessment systems and curricular program development. • Fundamental understanding of accreditation standards, regulatory expectations, and continuous quality improvement processes. • Experience contributing to accreditation preparation and review processes. • Deep expertise in program evaluation, learner assessment, data analysis, and quality improvement methodologies. • Evidence-informed approach to educational design and evaluation, with familiarity with the current literature and national landscape in competency-based medical education. • Track record of academic contributions that reflect intellectual rigor, creativity, and innovation in medical education. • Systems thinker with the ability to operate effectively across the medical school, university, and health system environments. • Forward-thinking in the use of technology, digital tools, and innovation in curricular design, assessment, and implementation. • Demonstrated ability to navigate complexity and ambiguity while translating strategy into effective execution. • Excellent communication and listening skills, with the ability to unite, inspire, and build consensus among students, faculty, staff, and institutional partners. • Mission-oriented and deeply committed to the future of medical education and to advancing student success and institutional excellence. • Collaborative relationship-building skills, with an ability to successfully partner and build consensus with key internal and external stakeholders at all levels of the organization and with external partners. Setting Strategy • The ability to create and articulate an inspiring vision for assessment and educational evaluation for the organization. • The inclination to seek and analyze data from a variety of sources to support assessment and educational evaluation decisions to align with the school’s strategic plan. • An entrepreneurial and creative approach to developing new, innovative ideas that will stretch the organization and push the boundaries within the industry. • The ability to effectively balance the desire/need for broad change with an understanding of how much change the organization is capable of handling, to create realistic goals and implementation plans that are achievable and successful. Executing for Results • The ability to set clear and challenging goals while committing the organization to improved performance; tenacious and accountable in driving results. • Comfortable with ambiguity and uncertainty; the ability to adapt nimbly and lead others through complex situations. • A risk-taker who seeks data and input from others to foresee possible threats or unintended circumstances from decisions; someone who takes smart risks. • A leader who is viewed by others as having a high degree of integrity and forethought in their approach to making decisions; the ability to act in a transparent and consistent manner while always taking into account what is best for the organization. Leading Teams • A leader who is self-reflective and aware of their own limitations; leads by example and drives the organization's performance with an attitude of continuous improvement by being open to feedback and self-improvement. • Naturally connects and builds strong and authentic relationships with others, demonstrating strong emotional intelligence and an ability to communicate clearly and persuasively. • The ability to persevere in the face of challenges, and exhibit a steadfast resolve and relentless commitment to higher standards, which elicits respect from followers. Nomination and Application Procedure To receive full consideration, interested individuals should electronically submit a Curriculum Vitae and a letter of interest to requisition number 26005809 via: https://www.join.pitt.edu. The letter of interest is a two to three-page cover letter detailing your experience and key achievements related to this position and your thoughts on how you see yourself contributing to the programs and responsibilities described in this position specification. Letters should be addressed to the University of Pittsburgh Associate Dean for Assessment and Educational Evaluation Search Committee and submitted electronically. Materials will be reviewed immediately and will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005525&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005525) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005525) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Dent Med-Periodontics/Preventive Dentistry - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005525 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Dental Medicine, with its Dental Hygiene Program in the Department of Periodontics and Preventive Dentistry, announces the immediate availability of one full-time (12-month) non-tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. Rank and salary are commensurate with education, teaching, and professional experience.  Candidates must be a graduate of a CODA-accredited dental hygiene program and have at least 5 years of clinical or professional experience; a master's degree or higher in a related field and at least 3 years teaching experience are preferred.  Candidates must also possess or be eligible for Pennsylvania dental hygiene licensure and a local anesthesia permit, and a background check is required prior to the official offer. Primary responsibilities include clinical, laboratory, and didactic instruction for the Dental Hygiene Associate Degree program, with additional duties that include committee work, student advising, scholarly activities, research, professional organization participation, community service, and faculty practice. Pitt Dental Medicine is located on the University main campus in Pittsburgh, contiguous with the other five health science schools. The school's general dental clinics and 11 specialty clinics play an integral role in improving the oral health of the patient population of southwestern Pennsylvania and beyond. As part of the clinical practice and faculty of the University of Pittsburgh, the practitioner will have the opportunity to collaborate with clinicians, innovators, and investigators from around the world and become part of a vibrant community of healthcare providers dedicated to making a difference in their chosen field and in the lives of others. Applicants should submit a letter of interest, a CV, and three letters of recommendation. Salary will be commensurate with experience and credentials. To apply, please go to join.pitt.edu, select Faculty Positions, and enter 26005525 in the keyword search. Please upload a curriculum vitae and a statement describing your interest in the position, qualifications, and experience. The search committee will begin reviewing applications upon receipt. Only applicants who appear best qualified will be invited for a personal interview. The candidate must provide at least three letters of recommendation. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005438&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Professor - Full-Time (26005438) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Professor - Full-Time (26005438) Job Description Faculty Professor - Full-Time Med-Pediatrics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005438 ) Qualified applicants seeking opportunities in clinical programs may find recruitment in The Department of Pediatrics of the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine Pediatric subspecialty programs: Our Subspecialties include: • Adolescent Medicine • Allergy • Bone Marrow Transplantation • Cardiology • Child Advocacy • Child Development • Hospitalists • Emergency Medicine • Endocrinology • Gastroenterology • General Academic Pediatrics • Hematology/Oncology • Infectious Diseases • Newborn Medicine • Neurology • Palliative Care and Supportive Medicine • Pulmonology • Rheumatology Job Description and Qualifications The position is for the recruitment of an Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor in the appointment (non-tenure) stream. Available positions are open to all applicants who hold a doctoral-level degree Education in the field of medicine (MD, DO), are board certified or board eligible, are qualified for medical licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, and meet the minimum position credentials for the pediatric specialty to provide clinical service. Responsibilities will include patient care, teaching, and research as determined by the chairman and the associated division chief. Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, and Professor positions in the appointment stream at the University of Pittsburgh, with rank and salary commensurate with experience and academic credentials. General rank requirements: Assistant Professors have 1-6 years of experience with demonstrated academic progress/contributions in their pediatric specialty; Associate Professors have 7-10 years of experience with significant demonstrated academic progress/contributions in their pediatric specialty; Professors have 10 or more years of experience with a clear demonstration of leadership, academic excellence and innovation in their pediatric specialty. Not all divisions have active recruitments; however, interested candidates can inquire about potential opportunities available in the Department of Pediatrics by applying to requisition number # 26005438 on Pitt Talent Center by visiting https://www.join.pitt.edu/ The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. See appended Job Posting The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
