    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006733&lang=en": {
      "title": "ADJUNCT FACULTY PROFESSOR - Domestic Arbitration",
      "description": "Job Description - ADJUNCT FACULTY PROFESSOR - Domestic Arbitration (26006733) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - ADJUNCT FACULTY PROFESSOR - Domestic Arbitration (26006733) Job Description ADJUNCT FACULTY PROFESSOR - Domestic Arbitration Law-Instruction - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006733 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Law invites applications for an adjunct faculty position to teach Domestic Arbitration for the spring 2027 semester. LAW 5675 - DOMESTIC ARBITRATION – 2 credits – Spring 2027 Description : This course will discuss not only the governing legal framework for domestic arbitration but also how to approach arbitration as a practitioner, with a particular focus on arbitrations in the employment and consumer contexts. Students will consider on what grounds arbitration can be compelled or, in the alternative, opposed. Students will also learn how arbitrations are actually conducted and the key practical differences between arbitration and litigations. The course will utilize simulations, role-playing exercises, mock arguments, and similar methodologies to ensure that students are active and engaged discussion participants. Salary : $2,500 per credit Qualifications : Juris Doctor degree, graduate-level teaching experience preferred; 5 years of practical experience in patent law and litigation preferred. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006721&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Professor Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Professor Assistant - Full-Time (26006721) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Professor Assistant - Full-Time (26006721) Job Description Faculty Professor Assistant - Full-Time Economics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006721 ) UNIVERSITY OF PITTSBURGH, DEPT. OF ECONOMICS is searching for an applied economist whose primary focus is scholarly work on East Asia, with a preference for China Studies, to fill the Thomas and Evelyn Rawski Endowed Chair in East Asian Studies. The position’s priority fields are environmental economics, public economics, and urban economics, while development economics, health economics, labor economics, macroeconomics, and trade will also be considered. The position will be effective Fall 2027, pending budgetary approval. We seek excellence in teaching and research. Salary, scholarly assistance, and benefits are competitive.  Complementarities with the research of current faculty are essential. Assistant Professor All Fields , with a preference for Environmental Economics, Public Economics, and Urban Economics, while Development Economics, Health Economics, Labor Economics, Macroeconomics, and Trade will also be considered PhD in economics required. Please apply at the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center AND at http://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ . To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 15, 2026. Applicants are required to submit a curriculum vitae and one research paper and arrange for the submission of three letters of recommendation. You may also submit a statement on research and teaching. Interviews will be held virtually. Recruiting Committee c/o Cindy Graf Department of Economics University of Pittsburgh cmg134@pitt.edu The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer. Please apply at the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center AND at http://www.aeaweb.org/joe/ . To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by November 15, 2026. Applicants are required to submit: a curriculum vitae; one research paper; and arrange for the submission of three letters of recommendation. You may also submit a statement on research and teaching. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006730&lang=en": {
      "title": "ADJUNCT FACULTY INSTRUCTOR - Online MSL Courses",
      "description": "Job Description - ADJUNCT FACULTY INSTRUCTOR - Online MSL Courses (26006730) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - ADJUNCT FACULTY INSTRUCTOR - Online MSL Courses (26006730) Job Description ADJUNCT FACULTY INSTRUCTOR - Online MSL Courses Law-Instruction - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006730 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Law (Pitt Law) seeks to hire part-time Adjunct Faculty to serve as course instructors in the online Master of Studies in Law (MSL) degree program beginning in spring 2027 and academic year 2026-2027. Instructors are sought for the following courses: American Legal System Contracts Torts Property Constitutional Law Criminal Law Legislation and Regulation Responsibilities : Course instructors support and guide student progress, provide detailed and substantive feedback on student submissions, grade assignments, tests, and exams. Instructors use existing online materials, tools, and procedures. Minimum Qualifications for Course Instructors : Licensed attorney with a minimum of 5 years of experience practicing or teaching law. At least 3 years of experience in the subject matter of the course for which they are engaged. Experience using Canvas or a similar learning management system and skill at online interaction. Proficiency in the use of Microsoft Outlook, Word, and Zoom. Applications : Applicants for a course instructor position MUST submit a CV and a cover letter. Please identify in your cover letter the specific course or courses you seek to instruct and document your suitability to teach each course for which you are applying. Salary : $1,000 per week of course instruction for an 8-week course, with a minimum of $5,333 for a 5-week course. he School of Law reserves the right not to offer the course in that term if fewer than 8 students are enrolled. In such a case, you retain your faculty position, but no compensation will be paid. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006740&lang=en": {
      "title": "ADJUNCT FACULTY PROFESSOR - Public Policy Seminar/Policy-Making Seminar ",
      "description": "Job Description - ADJUNCT FACULTY PROFESSOR - Public Policy Seminar/Policy-Making Seminar  (26006740) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - ADJUNCT FACULTY PROFESSOR - Public Policy Seminar/Policy-Making Seminar  (26006740) Job Description ADJUNCT FACULTY PROFESSOR - Public Policy Seminar/Policy-Making Seminar Law-Instruction - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006740 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Law is looking to hire an adjunct professor to teach the courses listed below in the spring of 2027. The courses are taught together to participating Law students as well as students in the Graduate School of Public and International Affairs (GSPIA). They are part of the Law School’s Semester in D.C. Program. The courses may be taught in person in our Washington, D.C. office or via Zoom. The courses will also be made available to Law students in Pittsburgh via synchronous technology. Students are required to write a policy research paper as one of the course requirements. PUBLIC POLICY SEMINAR (Law) - 3 credits / POLICY-MAKING SEMINAR (GSPIA) - 3 credits - Spring 2027 This seminar will explore the processes of federal law-making and public policy development through examination of a series of selected topics concerning lobbying, the legislative process, judicial challenges to new laws, and administrative rule-making and enforcement. A primary purpose of the seminar is to enrich students’ understanding of law-making and policy development by focusing on a series of case studies concerning particular laws and policies and introducing information about the relevant political dynamics, bureaucratic systems, and other real-world factors. Thus, in addition to studying written materials, students will talk with Washington-based attorneys and others who are experts in the relevant fields. The selected topics will vary from year to year. Salary : $2,500.00/credit Requirements: J.D.; at least three years' experience in legal aspects of public policy work, in relation to the federal government The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006678&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Associate Professor",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Associate Professor (26006678) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Associate Professor (26006678) Job Description Research Associate Professor Mechanical Engineering and Materials Science - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006678 ) The Mechanical Engineering and Materials Science Department at Pitt has state-of-the-art research and educational facilities and strong connections to local industry. Today, Pitt-MEMS features innovative undergraduate and graduate programs and world-class research in advanced manufacturing and design, materials for extreme conditions, soft matter biomechanics, computational and data-enabled engineering, cyber-physical systems and security, and nuclear and other sustainable energies. Our undergraduate and master’s students have an outstanding placement record at leading companies, and our doctoral students have successfully found faculty positions at major universities in the U.S. and abroad, as well as cutting-edge research positions in industry and national laboratories. Job Responsibilities Develop and conduct original research in advanced materials and technologies for energy storage and conversion, including the synthesis, characterization, and electrochemical evaluation of functional materials. Design, conduct, and lead experimental research involving advanced materials synthesis, processing, characterization, and electrochemical testing. Develop and evaluate materials and systems for applications including lithium-gas and solid-state batteries, hydrogen storage and conversion, electrocatalysis, and extreme conditions. Author and publish original research in peer-reviewed scientific journals and prepare technical reports documenting experimental methods, analyses, data and research findings. Develop and pursue sponsored research; lead and contribute to project conceptualization, proposal preparation, preliminary data generation, project execution, and technical reporting. Lead and coordinate research laboratory operations, including experimental activities, instrumentation, laboratory safety, and research planning. Provide research direction, training, and mentoring to graduate and undergraduate students and postdoctoral researchers, including instruction in experimental methods, instrumentation, data analysis, and scientific communication. Contribute to the development of intellectual property and technology-transfer activities arising from research, where applicable. Serve on appropriate research and faculty committees, graduate qualifying examination committees, and contribute to educational and program assessment activities. Job Requirements Ph.D. in Materials Science, Mechanical Engineering, Chemical Engineering, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research experience in advanced materials and energy storage and conversion systems, evidenced by peer-reviewed scientific publications and other scholarly contributions. Demonstrated expertise in materials synthesis, processing, and characterization for extreme conditions. Experience in conducting independent and interdisciplinary experimental research and analyzing and interpreting complex scientific data. Demonstrated ability to prepare scientific manuscripts, technical reports, research proposals, and presentations. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006423&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Instructor Adjunct",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Instructor Adjunct (26006423) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Instructor Adjunct (26006423) Job Description Faculty Instructor Adjunct SHRS-Physical Therapy - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006423 ) Position Description Adjunct Faculty in the Department of Physical Therapy The Department of Physical Therapy at the University of Pittsburgh, which is ranked number 7 in the US News and World Report, is currently recruiting adjunct faculty with a strong clinical background in physical therapy to teach in the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) Program. The faculty member will be committed to excellence in didactic and clinical education. The part-time 12-month appointment in the appointment stream will be at the rank of Adjunct Instructor. The Department is housed in the School of Health and Rehabilitation Sciences (SHRS), one of the six Schools of Health Sciences. We offer an entry-level professional Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) degree, which is currently offered in the traditional, on-campus format.  A hybrid format for the DPT degree is under development, which will offer distance online education complemented by on-campus immersion experiences. The Department also features a post-professional Master of Science degree and a Ph.D. in Rehabilitation Sciences, both in the on-campus format. We also offer the Primary Spine Practitioner (PSP) and the Advanced Vestibular Physical Therapist certificates, which are delivered in a hybrid format. Responsibilities for the Adjunct Faculty position include: • Online and in-person instruction and/or laboratory assistance • Collaborate with teaching faculty and leadership • Curriculum planning • Content development • Creation of assessment tools • Teaching support • Facilitations of small group break-out sessions/group discussions • Grading and evaluating student performance • Completing assessments • Proctoring exams • Providing ancillary support services for instructors as needed The University is especially interested in qualified candidates who can contribute, through their teaching, leadership, research, and/or service, to the excellence of the academic community. The applicant is expected to take full advantage of the Department’s strong and long-standing partnership with the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center, which is a world-class academic medical center in Pittsburgh. The ability to work with a highly productive team is critical to the success of this position. 2. Minimum objective qualifications; other desirable qualifications: Requirements for the position at the level of Adjunct Instructor: Earned entry-level professional PT degree from a CAPTE-accredited program with an active PT license in the United States; 4. Tenure/tenure-stream/appointment stream; full/part-time: This is an appointment stream, a part-time position. The time commitment varies by course. 5. Proposed starting date: November 1, 2026 6. Closing date for receipt of applications: Until the position is filled. 7. Name, address, and telephone number of the person to contact: To apply, send a curriculum vitae, to Lauren Lagana, Human Resources & Operations Manager, Department of Physical Therapy, lmb111@pitt.edu .  Also, please upload your CV to the Talent Center referencing requisition number 26006423. Please direct specific inquiries to Patrick Sparto, PT, Ph.D., ( psparto@pitt.edu ), Chair of the Search Committee. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006629&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006629) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006629) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006629 ) The Department of Medicine and Section of Palliative Care in the Division of General Internal Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking a full-time physician (MD/DO) in a relevant field with a focus on palliative care and serious illness at the level of Assistant Professor in the non-tenure stream. Candidates must have board certification or board eligibility in palliative medicine. The Section of Palliative Care is a multidisciplinary team committed to improving quality of life for patients and families through delivery of quality palliative care, education of palliative care skills and advancement in palliative care innovation. Our interdisciplinary palliative care team provides services across UPMC Presbyterian, UPMC Shadyside, UPMC Mercy, UPMC Magee-Womens Hospital, and outpatient clinics throughout the region. The team includes physicians, advanced practice providers, pharmacists, social workers, psychiatrists, and music therapists/counselors, each with specialized expertise in palliative care. Our fellowship program is nationally recognized and comprised of four fellowship tracks to accommodate diverse career goals. Responsibilities Include: Provide clinical care as the attending physician for the hospital-based palliative care consult service and deliver outpatient palliative care services in ambulatory clinic settings Contribute to the education and development of medical learners through clinical teaching, mentorship, and active participation in Palliative Care Grand Rounds and Journal Club activities Engage in scholarly activities that advance the field of palliative care, including research publications, abstract development and presentation, and delivery of invited lectures. Participate in service and leadership activities through committee and task force involvement, mentorship and coaching, peer review of scholarly manuscripts, and organizational leadership roles Applicants for Assistant Professor, non-tenure stream, should have three or more years of experience in the field of clinical and/or health services; have dispersed results through peer-reviewed publications and other scientific forums; have noteworthy teaching experience; and established the capability for continued career development, promotion, and tenure. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae for position #26006629 and apply using this link: http://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006405&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Part-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Part-Time (26006405) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Part-Time (26006405) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Part-Time Med-Critical Care Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006405 ) Department of Critical Care Medicine School of Medicine Faculty Position – BE/BC Pediatric Cardiac Critical Care Intensivist - Part-Time Description External: The Department of Critical Care Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh is actively seeking a part-time BE/BC intensivist to join our Pediatric Cardiac Critical Care Division faculty. Opportunities for clinicians, clinician-educators, and clinician-scientists are available. Candidates must possess outstanding communication and interpersonal skills and demonstrate a strong dedication to educating the next generation of clinicians. The ideal candidate will showcase exceptional clinical expertise, an ability to collaborate effectively with physician leaders from various specialties, and the aptitude to implement changes that align with best medical practices, institutional goals, and regulatory requirements. The candidate is expected to provide clinical care in one or more ICUs in the UPMC Health system; and actively participate in the education of fellows, residents, and students. Minimum objective qualifications ; other desirable qualifications : The selected candidate must have an MD or DO and be board-certified or board-eligible in Pediatric Critical Care Medicine by a US accreditation board. Dual board eligibility/certification in Cardiology or Advanced Cardiac Critical Care training is desirable. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills are required. The candidate should exhibit a strong commitment to educating the next generation of clinicians, advancing the field of pediatric cardiac critical care medicine through research, and advancing the ideals of diversity, equity, and inclusion in the health sciences. About the Department : Every year, physicians and families of more than 18,000 patients with heart disease choose the Heart Institute at CHP when they need the most advanced cardiac care. The CHP Heart Institute ranks as one of the top 10 US News and World Report Pediatric Cardiology and Heart Surgery programs in the United States. At the forefront are the 12-bed CICU and 21-bed CICU/Acute Care complex, especially designed to meet the needs of pediatric patients with both congenital and acquired heart disease. The CICU admits approximately 500 patients annually (children of all ages and adults) and specializes in perioperative management of patients with complex congenital heart disease, adult congenital heart disease, advanced management of patients with decompensated heart failure and pulmonary hypertension, including extracorporeal membrane oxygenation, ventricular assist devices, and heart and lung transplantation. The suitable candidate will join a dedicated and cohesive team of cardiac intensivists and pediatric advanced practice providers, and shall benefit from the mentorship, academic resources, and research opportunities offered by the Department of Critical Care Medicine, Safar Center for Resuscitation Research, and Center for Research, Investigation, and Systems Modeling of Acute Illness (CRISMA). Rank and/or title; salary range or minimum: Appointment rank of Assistant Professor, non-tenure is anticipated . Applicants are requested to submit their cover letter, curriculum vitae, and list of three references to Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh Requisition #26006405. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006149&lang=en": {
      "title": "Pediatric Urology",
      "description": "Job Description - Pediatric Urology (26006149) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Pediatric Urology (26006149) Job Description Pediatric Urology Med-Urology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006149 ) The Department of Urology at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine and the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC) is seeking a full-time faculty member. The position will include an appointment in the Department of Urology at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine as an Assistant or Associate Professor. Focused clinical responsibilities within a department of 40+ Clinical Urologists, will include attending duties in a large, integrated, multi-hospital clinical urology practice and educating students, residents, and fellows. The Candidate will be expected to provide pediatric urologic services within a growing practice in the metropolitan Pittsburgh area. Minimum Requirements: The Candidate must have an M.D. in Urology with appropriate board certification/eligibility; experience in a large hospital service is beneficial. Eligibility for medical licensure or practice in Pennsylvania is required. Completion of a Societies for Pediatric Urology (SPU)-Accredited fellowship is required. Qualified applicants are expected to have demonstrated excellence and commitment to patient care and experience with leading-edge diagnostic capabilities and delivery. Candidates at the Assistant Professor level should have 0 - 5 years of experience in clinical care and be committed to developing an academic career in clinical, transitional, or basic science research. Candidates at the Associate Professor level should have 6 - 9 years of experience and require evidence of significant educational or new clinical program development and/or a record of substantial clinical, translational, or basic science research. Recruitment is open until filled.  Salary commensurate with experience. Qualified applicants should apply via Talent Center under Requisition Number:  26006149 The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006269&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor ",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor  (26006269) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor  (26006269) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor Med-Biomedical Informatics - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006269 ) The Department of Biomedical Informatics (DBMI) ( https://www.dbmi.pitt.edu ) at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine is recruiting faculty in biomedical informatics for appointment stream, tenure-track and tenured positions . The University of Pittsburgh has more than 40 years of history in applying artificial intelligence and machine learning (AI/ML) to biomedical informatics, from some of the earliest work in medical decision support and expert systems to current efforts to develop and apply AI/ML across clinical and health informatics, clinical research informatics, population health informatics, translational bioinformatics, and imaging informatics. This work spans anesthesiology, critical care, neurology, pediatrics, oncology, infectious diseases, and other domains. We seek creative, productive, and collaborative colleagues who will build on this legacy by applying informatics and AI/ML methods to fundamental biomedical questions and by engaging in team science. We are particularly interested in expertise in multimodal data analysis, clinical imaging, target trial emulation, analysis of complex molecular data, clinical decision support, implementation science, and research evidence support tools. The ideal candidate will be an accomplished scholar working at the intersection of AI/ML and biomedical informatics, with one or more active federally funded research projects. Candidates must hold either a PhD (in fields including, but not limited to, biomedical informatics, health informatics, bioinformatics, computer science, statistics, or information science) or a professional health degree (e.g., MD, RN, PharmD) with informatics training. We welcome clinicians, including internists, pediatricians, surgeons, psychiatrists, nurses, and pharmacists, particularly those with an AI/ML research track record and an interest in clinical informatics, precision medicine, or public health informatics. For an Assistant Professor position candidates must hold a doctoral or appropriate professional degree and have fewer than five years of relevant experience. They should demonstrate effective teaching ability, experience in advanced study and research, or professional expertise that enables them to make meaningful academic contributions. Candidates should also show promise of originality and excellence in their field of scholarship, as well as the ability to guide, mentor, and support students. For an Associate Professor position, qualifications are as follows: to the degree requirements above, candidates should have five or more years of experience, substantial experience in teaching and research, eminence in a scholarly or professional field, and a track record of securing external funding. For a Professor position, qualifications are as follows: In addition to the degree requirements above, candidates should have ten or more years of experience, authoritative knowledge and a strong reputation in a recognized field of learning, and effective teaching skills. They should have attained superior stature in their field through research, scholarship, professional leadership, and sustained funding. Instructions to apply Applicants should apply through the online University of Pittsburgh Talent Center (requisition number 26006269 ) using the following link: https://www.join.pitt.edu/ The following four documents are required for an application: (1) Cover letter (maximum 1 page); (2) Curriculum vitae; (3) Research Statement, describing planned research and plans for securing external funding ( maximum 3 pages, not including bibliography); (4) Teaching and Mentoring Statement ( maximum 1 page). Applicants should submit the following materials in one combined PDF file. This is an in-person position; candidates must be located in or willing to relocate to Pittsburgh, PA. Applications submitted by November 1, 2027, will receive full consideration. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Teaching Statement, Other (see posting for additional details) Optional Attachments : Research Statement Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006215&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006215) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006215) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-OB-Gyn & Reproductive Science - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006215 ) The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking a full-time physician to be hired at the academic rank of Assistant Professor, appointment stream. This is an excellent opportunity for a board-certified OB/GYN to join a well-established OB/GYN Department. The OB/GYN department is home to an academic obstetrics and gynecology residency program with a total of 40 OB/GYN residents, as well as subspecialty fellowships in maternal-fetal medicine, urogynecology, reproductive endocrinology and infertility, medical genetics, gynecologic oncology, minimally invasive surgery, infectious diseases, and family planning. The Physician will allocate 80% of their professional effort to providing OB/GYN clinical care, including services at Magee-Womens Hospital, outpatient visits at satellite offices, and patient care in ambulatory settings. Responsibilities will also include office coverage, on‑call duties, and other clinical activities as reasonably assigned by the Chair of the Department. The remaining 20% of the Physician's effort will be dedicated to teaching, research and service within the School of Medicine, with a primary focus on research. Qualifications: MD or DO is required. Board certification in obstetrics and gynecology Demonstrated teaching ability and experience in advanced study and research. Minimum of two years of experience in guiding and mentoring students. Minimum of two years of clinical experience with patients in an outpatient and hospital setting. Applicants should apply through the Talent Center at htps://www.join.pit.edu, using Requisition #26006215 The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=25000717&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Professor Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Professor Assistant - Full-Time (25000717) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Professor Assistant - Full-Time (25000717) Job Description Faculty Professor Assistant - Full-Time Med-Anesthesiology and Perioperative Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 25000717 ) Assistant Professor The University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine, Department of Anesthesiology and Perioperative Medicine is recruiting a full-time faculty member at the Assistant Professor level. Qualifications: •    Medical degree in Anesthesiology •    Eligible for an unrestricted Pennsylvania medical license •    Board-eligible or Board-certified •    Completion of accredited residency and fellowship specialty training •    The ability to work with a highly productive team is critical to the success of this position The ideal candidate will be committed to excellence in clinical care, teaching, and/or research. Our diverse anesthesiology group provides a variety of challenging cases for generalists and other anesthesiology specialists. We are seeking highly talented applicants to join our healthcare system and offer opportunities in the subspecialties of neuro, cardiac, and general anesthesia throughout a seventeen-hospital system. Academic rank [Assistant Professor (0-5 years of experience)] is commensurate with prior academic achievements and experience. Qualified applicants should apply via the Talent Center. Requisition # 25000717 N/A The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Optional Attachments : Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006475&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Philosophy (26006475) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Philosophy (26006475) Job Description Assistant Professor of Philosophy Philosophy - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006475 ) The Department of Philosophy seeks an Assistant Professor for a tenure stream faculty position, pending budgetary approval.  Proposed starting date is August 15, 2027. Area of Specialization: Modern Philosophy or Ethics, Practical Philosophy broadly construed Responsibilities:  Undergraduate and graduate teaching, and regular departmental duties. Applicants should submit a CV (including a dissertation abstract or research statement), letters of recommendation, evidence of teaching ability, and a writing sample. *IMPORTANT NOTE*- Please DO NOT upload letters of recommendation to the application website. Rather, please have all letters sent to Estelle Burris at eburris@pitt.edu. Required Qualifications: (1) A PhD in Philosophy or a closely related field expected by the proposed start date; (2) a promising research agenda. Applications received by November 6, 2026 will receive full consideration. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Please direct all further inquiries to Brian Deutsch, briandeutsch@pitt.edu. Department of Philosophy University of Pittsburgh 1017 Cathedral of Learning Pittsburgh, PA 15260 Applicants should submit a CV (including a dissertation abstract or research statement), letters of recommendation, evidence of teaching ability, and a writing sample. *IMPORTANT NOTE*- Please DO NOT upload letters of recommendation to the application website. Rather, please have all letters sent to Estelle Burris at eburris@pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
