n pump therapy. The role requires clinical judgment, advanced hemodynamic management, effective communication, and the ability to work closely with cardiac surgery, thoracic surgery, cardiology, heart failure, transplant, perfusion, advanced practice providers, nursing, respiratory therapy, pharmacy, and other members of the multidisciplinary team. Primary responsibilities include providing clinical coverage in the CTICU at UPMC Presbyterian; leading multidisciplinary ICU rounds; developing and implementing evidence-based diagnostic and therapeutic plans; supervising and teaching fellows, residents, medical students, and advanced practice providers; maintaining timely and accurate documentation; participating in quality improvement, patient safety, and operational initiatives; and supporting an inclusive learning and clinical environment. Faculty may also have opportunities to provide clinical care in other ICUs across the UPMC Health System based on departmental needs, clinical expertise, and mutual agreement. Minimum objective qualifications; other desirable qualifications: Applicants must hold an MD or DO degree, be board-certified or board-eligible in critical care medicine by a United States accreditation board and be eligible for medical licensure in Pennsylvania. Base training may include internal medicine, emergency medicine, surgery, anesthesiology, neurology, or another relevant discipline with accredited critical care training. Required qualifications include excellent communication skills, professionalism, sound clinical judgment, and a commitment to teamwork, education, patient-centered care, and a respectful and inclusive academic environment. Prior clinical experience or focused training in cardiothoracic critical care, ECMO, mechanical circulatory support, advanced hemodynamic management, perioperative cardiothoracic care, echocardiography, quality improvement, education, or clinical research is desirable but not required. About the Department: The Department of Critical Care Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine is the nation’s first and one of the foremost stand-alone academic departments devoted to critical care medicine. In partnership with UPMC, department faculty provide state-of-the-art multidisciplinary care for critically ill adult and pediatric patients across the UPMC Health System. The department is also a national leader in critical care education, faculty development, quality improvement, and research, with programs that span clinical care, translational science, population health, implementation science, and health services research. Rank and/or title; salary range or minimum: Academic appointment will be at the rank of Professor in the non-tenure stream, commensurate with qualifications, experience, and academic accomplishments. Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, list of three references, and any required application materials through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center, position 26005954. Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh - join.pitt.edu. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006518&lang=en": {
      "title": "Family Nurse Practitioner Nursing Faculty - Full Time - Non-Tenure Stream",
      "description": "Job Description - Family Nurse Practitioner Nursing Faculty - Full Time - Non-Tenure Stream (26006518) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Family Nurse Practitioner Nursing Faculty - Full Time - Non-Tenure Stream (26006518) Job Description Family Nurse Practitioner Nursing Faculty - Full Time - Non-Tenure Stream Nurs-Health Promotion & Development - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006518 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing is seeking qualified applicants for a full-time, non-tenure stream, Family Nurse Practitioner faculty position in the Department of Health Promotion and Development. This Appointment-Stream position will be a full-time faculty member in the Health Promotion and Development department in the School of Nursing, who will be responsible for teaching, clinical instruction, scholarship, and service. Responsibilities will include teaching and mentoring students in both the classroom and clinical setting, contributing to course development and delivery, and supporting student learning, professional development, and readiness for practice. Expectations also include active and sustained engagement in scholarship, clinical innovation, and dissemination through publications and presentations. The faculty member will also participate in service activities that support the School, University, profession, and community, contributing to committees, professional organizations, clinical partnerships, and community-based initiatives in alignment with the mission of the institution. Other duties may be assigned based on department needs. Faculty members receive dedicated time and resources to ensure they can successfully conduct their program of research, disseminate their research, and develop professionally. Faculty promotion opportunities are available for all ranks. Qualifications for these non-tenure stream faculty positions include a doctorate in nursing and eligibility for RN licensure in Pennsylvania. Salary and academic rank are commensurate with qualifications and experience. Faculty Requirements in the Appointment Stream (Non-Tenure Stream): · Assistant Professor – A) An earned doctorate in nursing or a field related to the area of scholarship within the School of Nursing is required. B) Demonstrated expertise in the indicated area of family nurse practitioner nursing; C) Certification as an Family Nurse Practitioner or eligibility to sit for a board exam; D) Evidence of or potential for a sustained and impactful program of scholarship. E) Evidence of or potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring, and contributing to a learning environment that values evidence-based practice. · Associate Professor – A) An earned doctorate in nursing or a field related to the area of scholarship within the School of Nursing is required. B) Demonstrated expertise in the indicated area of family nurse practitioner nursing; C) Certification as an Family Nurse Practitioner or eligibility to sit for a board exam; D) Evidence of a sustained and impactful program of scholarship that is nationally recognized. E) Evidence of excellence in teaching and mentoring, and contributing to a learning environment that values evidence-based practice. F) Evidence of or potential for leadership in the field. · Professor – A) An earned doctorate in nursing or a field related to the area of scholarship within the School of Nursing is required. B) Demonstrated expertise in the indicated area of family nurse practitioner nursing; C) Certification as an Family Nurse Practitioner or eligibility to sit for a board exam; D) Evidence of a sustained and impactful program of scholarship that is internationally recognized. E) Evidence of excellence in teaching and mentoring, and contributing to a learning environment that values evidence-based practice. F) Evidence of leadership in the field. About the University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing : Since its founding in 1939, the University of Pittsburgh School of Nursing has provided faculty and students with the resources and support to generate new healthcare knowledge and the educational foundation to conduct evidence-based practice, engage in scholarly activities, and translate knowledge to improve the delivery of healthcare in Pennsylvania, the nation, and throughout the world. As one of the nation's elite schools of nursing, Pitt Nursing receives millions of dollars in NIH grant funding each year, and U.S. News & World Report highly ranks multiple academic programs. A complete list of rankings for the School of Nursing can be found at: www.nursing.pitt.edu/about/our-rankings. About the University of Pittsburgh : Named a \"New Ivy\" by Forbes, the University of Pittsburgh is internationally recognized as a center of learning, innovation, and research. Pitt shares a campus with the world-class healthcare enterprise, UPMC. Collaboration between Pitt and UPMC results in an environment of interdisciplinary research and education, cutting-edge evidence-based practice, and an infrastructure that fosters career development and sustained successes. Apply Now : Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Candidates should apply online at https://www.join.pitt.edu/ and search for requisition number: 26006518. For more information on the School of Nursing, visit www.nursing.pitt.edu. As part of your application, please provide a statement of your area of scholarship and why you believe you will be successful at Pitt Nursing. Reasons to work at Pitt : The University offers exceptional benefits that include education benefits, health and wellness benefits, and a generous retirement plan. There are also generous tuition and educational benefits. Information about these and other benefits can be found on the University's HR website: Benefits | Human Resources | University of Pittsburgh As part of your application, please provide a statement of your area of scholarship and why you believe you will be successful at Pitt Nursing. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006524&lang=en": {
      "title": "Executive in Residence in Business for Health, Technology and Impact (BHTI)",
      "description": "Job Description - Executive in Residence in Business for Health, Technology and Impact (BHTI) (26006524) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Executive in Residence in Business for Health, Technology and Impact (BHTI) (26006524) Job Description Executive in Residence in Business for Health, Technology and Impact (BHTI) BUS-Grad Business Administration - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006524 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Business is seeking a current or former senior leader with extensive executive or upper-management experience in healthcare administration to support its Business for Health, Technology and Impact (BHTI) initiative. The successful candidate will bring at least 10 years of healthcare industry experience with leadership roles, experience, and professional relationships to help Pitt Business develop and implement executive education programs at the intersection of business, health, and technology. Pitt Business invites applications from interested professionals for a part-time position as an Executive in Residence (EIR). The EIR will be responsible for: Identifying relevant healthcare subject matter experts and industry leaders and connecting them with the BHTI initiative. Providing guidance on healthcare industry education needs to inform the development of executive education curricula and non-credit certificate programs. Assisting with BHTI strategies for marketing, fundraising, partnership development, and outreach. Supporting the development of the BHTI Ambassador Program by building and maintaining relationships with healthcare administration professionals throughout the region. Supporting the development of relationships and partnerships with healthcare organizations and other external stakeholders. Working closely with the Associate Dean for Research and Strategic Initiatives to support the continued development and improvement of BHTI. Performing other related duties as needed in support of the BHTI initiative. This is a part-time appointment with a 12-month term beginning on January 1, 2027. Interested applicants should upload a resume with their application. The resume should demonstrate the applicant’s relevant professional experience, expertise, and qualifications. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006538&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006538) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006538) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Physics & Astronomy - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006538 ) Faculty Position in Astrophysics University of Pittsburgh Department of Physics and Astronomy The Department of Physics and Astronomy at the University of Pittsburgh ( http://www.physicsandastronomy.pitt.edu/ ) invites applications for a new faculty member in the field of Astrophysics. This tenure-stream position will be at the Assistant Professor level, starting on or after August 15, 2027, subject to budgetary approval. Applicants should have a PhD in Astrophysics or similar discipline. We are seeking applications from all sub-fields of astrophysics, with a particular interest in candidates who will complement and extend current research strengths in astrophysical surveys, stellar astrophysics, theoretical cosmology, and extragalactic astronomy. The department is a member of the LSST Discovery Alliance and the Simons Observatory and participates in the Dark Energy Spectroscopic Instrument, the LSST Dark Energy Science Collaboration, Sloan Digital Sky Survey, Subaru Prime Focus Spectrograph, and Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope Core Community projects. Faculty are also active users of national supercomputers and observing facilities (e.g., HST, JWST).  Successful candidates should have a demonstrated record of research success, a vision for their future research program, and potential effective teaching at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. To ensure full consideration, complete applications should be received by December 1, 2026, but applications will continue to be accepted for the duration of the search. Applicants can apply online at www.join.pitt.edu . Candidates should submit (1) A brief cover letter (2) A CV which includes: lists of invited talks; grant, telescope, and computing time applications; leadership and mentoring activities. (3) A research statement (4) A publication list (5) A brief statement of teaching and community-building interests and experience (6) At least three letters of reference to slogan@pitt.edu The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer. For questions please contact Professor Rachel Bezanson (chair of the search committee, rachel.bezanson@pitt.edu ) or Professor Andrew Zentner (department chair, phyast-chair@pitt.edu ) The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation, Teaching Statement, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006006&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006006) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006006) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Pathology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006006 ) RANK/TITLE: Assistant Professor (1-5 years of experience) appointment stream DEPARTMENT/DIVISION: Department of Pathology University of Pittsburgh, Division of Breast and Gynecologic Pathology, UPMC Magee-Womens Hospital DESCRIPTION OF WORK: · The Women’s pathology division at Magee-Womens Hospital is the department’s centerpiece women care facility where all breast, gynecologic, placental/perinatal specimens and gynecologic cytology is received and processed for diagnostic purposes. · Responsibilities will include sign out of breast and gynecologic surgical pathology and possibly gynecologic cytology (Pap tests) specimens, teaching and training residents, medical students, and fellows. · The division faculty interprets and report 26,000 women’s surgical pathology specimens, and ~45,000 gynecologic cytology specimens. · Division’s clinical research focuses on immunohistochemistry, gynecologic cytology, image analysis, and molecular approaches to gynecologic and breast malignancies, and perinatal pathology. · Opportunities to support basic research at Magee-Womens Research Institute through the development of peer-reviewed funded research programs and collaborative opportunities with faculty engaged in molecular biology, genomics, proteomics, etc. · Teaching opportunities available with medical students in the School of Medicine, pathology fellows, and residents. JOB DUTIES: · Sign out breast and gynecologic surgical pathology · Sign out gynecologic cytology (Pap tests) specimens, if proficient · Teach Pathology fellows and Pathology residents · Participate in translational research initiatives · Participate in department QA program. QUALIFICATIONS: · M.D. degree · Pennsylvania medical license · Residency training in Anatomic Pathology · Experience and/or fellowship training in breast/gynecologic surgical pathology · Experience and/or fellowship training in cytopathology SALARY AND BENEFITS: Salary will be commensurate with experience. The individual will be a full-time faculty member at the University of Pittsburgh, as well as a participant in the UPMC/UPP faculty practice plan. APPLICATION: To apply: Go to TALENT CENTER at www.join.pitt.edu and search for requisition 26006006 in the keyword. For questions contact: Rohit Bhargava, M.B.B.S. Chief of Pathology, UPMC Magee-Womens Hospital ( bharrx@upmc.edu ). The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006318&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26006318) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time (26006318) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Full-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006318 ) The Division of Geriatric Medicine in the Department of Medicine at the University of Pittsburgh / UPMC invites applications for a dynamic physician leader to serve as Associate Chief of Clinical Affairs. This role offers the opportunity to shape and advance an innovative, multi-setting clinical enterprise that cares for older adults across the full continuum, from acute inpatient settings to community and long-term care. The position rank will be Associate Professor or Professor in the Non-Tenure Stream based on the candidate's qualifications. Applicants should hold an MD or equivalent degree and be board certified in Geriatric Medicine with a demonstrated record of clinical excellence and leadership. Experience in program development, quality improvement, and team mentorship is strongly preferred. Responsibilities Include: Lead and integrate clinical operations across inpatient geriatric consultation services, comprehensive outpatient practices, and post-acute / long-term care partnerships throughout the UPMC network. Champion the GUIDE Model (Guiding an Improved Dementia Experience), a CMS innovation program delivering coordinated, dementia-specific care that supports patients and caregivers at home and in the community. Provide strategic oversight of the Hospital Elder Life Program (HELP), our evidence-based initiative to prevent delirium and functional decline in hospitalized older adults. Collaborate with the Division Chief and Fellowship Program Director to sustain and grow the ACGME-accredited Geriatric Medicine Fellowship, mentoring the next generation of geriatricians. Drive quality improvement, patient safety, and value-based care initiatives across all clinical sites, with direct impact on outcomes for one of the nation’s largest older adult populations. Build interdisciplinary teams to deliver patient and family-centered care. Applicants for Associate Professor, non-tenure stream, should have five or more years of experience in related scientific research; have independent, external research funding and a substantial record of peer-reviewed publications; have significant teaching experience; and demonstrate the capacity for sustained, impactful, and independent scholarly contributions and leadership. Applicants for Professor, non-tenure stream, will have served five to seven years as Associate Professor. The rank of professor recognizes the attainment of authoritative knowledge and reputation in a recognized field of learning and the achievement of effective teaching skills. The professor should have attained superior stature in their field through scholarship, professional practice, and leadership in professional and learned organizations. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae for position #26006318 and apply using this link:  http://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006265&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (26006265) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (26006265) Job Description Research Assistant Professor Med-Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006265 ) The Department of Surgery at the University of Pittsburgh is inviting applications for the faculty position of Research Assistant Professor. The faculty member will play a key role in collaborative research programs applying cutting-edge imaging and molecular technologies to regenerative medicine, wound healing, and vascular repair at the McGowan Institute for Regenerative Medicine (MIRM). QUALIFICATIONS •    Must have a doctoral degree (Ph.D.) in Biological Sciences, Biochemistry, Cell/Molecular Biology, or a related field. •    Demonstrated expertise in diabetic and chronic wound healing, including impaired-perfusion and ischemic wound models, using in vivo rodent models and human tissue. •    Specific experience with cutaneous vascular biology — angiogenesis, vasculogenesis, endothelial and fibroblast reprogramming, and in vivo tissue-perfusion assessment. •    Hands-on experience with cutting-edge imaging technologies applied to skin and vasculature, such as in vivo wound-perfusion imaging (e.g., laser speckle), high-resolution confocal and multiphoton microscopy, and single-cell molecular profiling of tissue. •    Experience with epigenetic and gene-regulatory approaches — DNA methylation/demethylation (e.g., TET-mediated), RNA methylation, epigenetic gene editing, and epithelial–mesenchymal transition biology. •    Experience with primary skin cell and ex vivo/organotypic skin work (fibroblast, endothelial, and keratinocyte culture and reprogramming). •    5+ years of research experience in an academic research environment. •    Must be willing to work with animals and human subjects. •    Must be able to multitask and show interest in contributing to several concurrent projects in the Center. •    Tissue Nanotransfection (TNT) technology experience required. •    Electronic Lab Notebook (e.g., LabGuru) experience preferred. RESPONSIBILITIES The qualified scientist will play a major role in a dynamic program in basic and translational research applying cutting-edge imaging and molecular reprogramming technologies to regenerative medicine, wound healing, and vascular repair at MIRM. The faculty member will use pre-clinical rodent models — supported by advanced in vivo perfusion imaging and single-cell/spatial molecular profiling — to study impaired diabetic and ischemic wound healing and to develop tissue-reprogramming and epigenetic gene-editing strategies (including TNT-based approaches) that restore perfusion and drive tissue repair. As this is a supporting role, the faculty member will partner with interdisciplinary scientists toward translational program building but will not be expected to have regular teaching or service responsibilities external to their research group. A successful candidate will also actively support grant submissions and submit grants as PI. We offer a competitive academic salary, fringe benefits, and state-of-the-art facilities. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. To apply, upload a current CV, cover letter, and letters of reference to requisition number: 26006265  at https:// www.join.pitt.edu The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006397&lang=en": {
      "title": "Visiting Fellowship",
      "description": "Job Description - Visiting Fellowship (26006397) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Visiting Fellowship (26006397) Job Description Visiting Fellowship Center for Philosophy of Science - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006397 ) Visiting Fellows Program The Visiting Fellows Program offers philosophers of science the opportunity to spend a term or full two-term academic year at the Center, and we welcome applications from all interested candidates. Visiting Fellows are not required to teach, serve on committees, or take on administrative responsibilities. They are, however, expected to pursue their own research, give a lunchtime talk, participate in the Center's intellectual life by attending talks and discussions, reside in Pittsburgh, and make regular use of their offices. Fall fellowships run from September 1 through December, and Spring fellowships run from early January through the end of April. Fellows are expected to participate for the full semester. Eligibility Applicants must hold a doctoral degree, typically in philosophy, history, or philosophy of science, or hold an established position within the professional philosophy of science community. In special cases, the Center will consider applicants with doctorates in other fields, though such applicants should be aware that their chances of acceptance are lower. Funding The Center expects a Visiting Fellow's research to be supported by their home institution, a foundation, or a government agency. The Center's monthly stipend is intended to help offset the additional costs of relocation, not to serve as primary funding. Terms of Residence The Center's academic terms are Fall (September 1–December 31) and Spring (January 1–April 30); the two-term academic year comprises both. The Center discourages visits for periods shorter than a full term or the full academic year. With prior written arrangement, Fellows may, depending on eligibility, remain in residence through the summer, though the Center is unable to provide a stipend or office support during this period. Separate arrangements can be made for scholars wishing to work in the Archives of Scientific Philosophy over the summer. Returning Fellows Policy A Fellow may visit the Center for a maximum of two semesters within any ten-year period. In practice, this means that after an initial semester-long fellowship, a Fellow may return for one additional semester within the following ten years. A Fellow who has completed a full academic year at the Center must wait ten years before returning. After ten years, eligibility resets. Application Requirements A cover letter indicating that a Visiting Fellowship is being sought, specifying the proposed period of residence, any prior fellowships held at the Center, if applicable - the source and amount of anticipated external funding. A project description (500–1,000 words) outlining the work to be undertaken during the fellowship. A curriculum vitae. A writing sample, or a link to one. Three letters of reference from scholars familiar with your work. We recommend that letters be blinded to the applicant. Letters should be sent to pittcntr@pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Other (see posting for additional details) Optional Attachments : Research Statement Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006574&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Professor - Part-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Part-Time (26006574) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Professor - Part-Time (26006574) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Professor - Part-Time Med-Medicine - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006574 ) The Division of Classical Hematology, in the Department of Medicine, at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine and University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC) is seeking an exceptional candidate for the position of Professor of Medicine in the appointment stream focused on a part-time academic practice in classical hematology. The ideal candidate has interests in outpatient clinical and research in hemostasis, thrombosis, Porphyria and or hemoglobinopathies. The primary responsibilities of this position will be to develop and lead research studies and to support continuity, collaboration, and visibility for the Division of Classical Hematology. Applicants will have an MD degree and will have served five to seven years as Associate Professor. The rank of professor recognizes the attainment of authoritative knowledge and reputation in a recognized field of learning and the achievement of effective teaching skills. The professor should have attained superior stature in their field through scholarship, professional practice, and leadership in professional and learned organizations. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae and apply to requisition number 26006574 via: https://www.join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005925&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Research - Instructor- Department of Surgery",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Research - Instructor- Department of Surgery (26005925) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Research - Instructor- Department of Surgery (26005925) Job Description Faculty Research - Instructor- Department of Surgery Med-Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005925 ) The Department of Surgery, the McGowan Institute for Regenerative Medicine, the Trivedi Institute for Space and Global Biomedicine, and the High-Throughput Genome Center (HTGC) at the University of Pittsburgh are seeking a highly motivated Research Instructor in the appointment stream. This is a full-time position at the exciting intersection of space biomedicine, trauma research, and multi-omics technologies, with close integration into the University of Pittsburgh's High-Throughput Genome Center (HTGC) core facility. Qualifications As a Research Instructor in the appointment stream, the successful candidate must hold a Master’s or equivalent degree in biochemistry, analytical chemistry, biotechnology, or a related field; candidates nearing completion of a master’s degree with strong, directly relevant research experience will also be considered. We are particularly interested in individuals who bring a combination of analytical, computational, and translational strengths, including expertise in one or more of the following areas: •    Lipidomics and/or metabolomics using LC-MS/MS and HPLC-based workflows, including method development, extraction optimization, and quantification of lipid and metabolite biomarkers in complex biological matrices such as plasma and extracellular vesicles •    Isolation, characterization, and analysis of extracellular vesicles (EVs) from plasma or other biofluids •    Proteomics workflows and mass-spectrometry-based protein identification and quantification •    NMR-based metabolomics, including spectral acquisition, processing, and open-source pipeline development, is highly desirable •    Bioinformatics and chemometric approaches for multi-omics data integration and biomarker discovery •    Interest or experience in trauma biology, radiation biology, or spaceflight and microgravity research •    Excellent scientific writing and communication skills, with a track record of peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations. The ideal candidate thrives at the interface of analytical chemistry and translational biomedicine, and is excited about applying lipidomic, proteomic, metabolomic, and NMR expertise to questions that span from low-Earth orbit to trauma and human disease. Job Summary This Research Instructor in the appointment stream position offers a rare opportunity to lead and support multi-omics research at the frontier of space biomedicine and trauma biology, within one of the most dynamic and internationally connected environments in the field. The successful candidate will work closely with the University of Pittsburgh's High-Throughput Genome Center (HTGC), leveraging its lipidomics, proteomics, metabolomics, and NMR platforms alongside a lab with deep roots in NASA-funded multi-omics research and NIH/DoD trauma research. The Research Instructor in the appointment stream will contribute to a broad and exciting portfolio of federally funded and industry-supported research programs, including: •    Space radiation and trauma lipidomics, characterizing how space radiation and traumatic injury alter the lipid composition of plasma and extracellular vesicles, including comparative analyses with biological samples from commercial spaceflight missions such as SpaceX's Inspiration4 •    Multi-omic biomarker discovery, identifying lipid, protein, and metabolite biomarkers associated with mitochondrial dysfunction, immune dysregulation, and tissue injury across spaceflight, trauma, and post-viral disease models •    NMR metabolomics pipeline development, building and refining open-source NMR metabolomics workflows for spaceflight-relevant and trauma datasets. •    Core facility integration, supporting sample processing, LC-MS/MS and NMR data acquisition, and analytical pipeline development through the HTGC, in collaboration with core staff and users across the university The Research Instructor will be embedded within the McGowan Institute for Regenerative Medicine, Trivedi Institute for Space and Global Biomedicine, Department of Surgery, and HTGC., a collaborative environment with strong ties to NASA, ESA, DoD, NIH, and global biomedical research networks. The candidate will be expected to support analytical research projects, contribute to grant development and manuscript preparation, mentor students and trainees, and help maintain and advance shared LC-MS/MS and NMR instrumentation and protocols. The initial appointment is for one year, with the strong expectation of renewal for one to two additional years based on performance and funding availability. Application Information To be considered for this position, please submit a current curriculum vitae through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center at join.pitt.edu and search for Requisition #: 26005925 The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006376&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006376) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26006376) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-OB-Gyn & Reproductive Science - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006376 ) The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Science - Magee Women's Research Institute at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking full-time faculty at the level of Assistant Professor, tenure stream. Qualified applicants will be established investigators with a proven track record in extramural NIH funding. Exciting opportunities are available for translational research and clinical care.  This position involves Research, Teaching, and Service activities. Qualified applicants must have a PhD in a medical field of study. Magee-Womens Research Institute (MWRI) is an independent research Institute and one of the largest in the nation that focuses on reproductive biology, and women's and infants' health.  Since its inception in 1992, MWRI has been a leader in funding from the National Institute of Health (NIH) and other sources. Opportunities are available to work with members of MWRI on specific research projects. Time to pursue individual research is available. Expected to establish and maintain an innovative, externally funded research program in reproductive biology that advances our understanding of the molecular, cellular, and developmental mechanisms underlying women's reproductive health across the lifespan. The research is expected to leverage state-of-the-art approaches in genomics, epigenetics, developmental biology, and reproductive science to generate new biological insights and identify opportunities for improved prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of reproductive disorders.  Expected to collaborate closely with investigators at MWRI, the Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Sciences, and the broader University of Pittsburgh research community to foster interdisciplinary and translational research. Expected to participate fully in the scientific activities of MWRI, including attending institute conferences and seminars, contributing to collaborative research and grant development, mentoring trainees, and enhancing the national and international reputation of MWRI. Candidates should apply at www.join.pitt.edu under requisition #26006376. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer.. Position requires a PhD in a medical field of study. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
