research program in reproductive biology that advances our understanding of the molecular, cellular, and developmental mechanisms underlying women's reproductive health across the lifespan. The research is expected to leverage state-of-the-art approaches in genomics, epigenetics, developmental biology, and reproductive science to generate new biological insights and identify opportunities for improved prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of reproductive disorders.  Expected to collaborate closely with investigators at MWRI, the Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Sciences, and the broader University of Pittsburgh research community to foster interdisciplinary and translational research. Expected to participate fully in the scientific activities of MWRI, including attending institute conferences and seminars, contributing to collaborative research and grant development, mentoring trainees, and enhancing the national and international reputation of MWRI. Candidates should apply at www.join.pitt.edu under requisition #26006053. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer.. Position requires a PhD in a medical field of study. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
