    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006473&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time (26006473) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time (26006473) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Associate - Full-Time Med-Office of the Dean - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006473 ) Faculty Positions in Space and Global Biomedicine Assistant Professor or Associate Professor, Tenure Stream Trivedi Institute for Space and Global Biomedicine University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine The University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine's Trivedi Institute for Space and Global Biomedicine invites applications for full-time faculty positions at the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor level in the tenure stream. The Trivedi Institute is an interdisciplinary research institute bringing together space science, engineering, biology, and medicine to advance biomedical discovery and innovation. The Institute uses spaceflight and space-relevant environments as platforms for understanding biology, developing new medical technologies, and translating discoveries into solutions that benefit human health on Earth and beyond. The Institute's mission spans fundamental discovery, translational innovation, and the development of approaches relevant to human health and resilience in space, terrestrial, and resource-constrained environments. We seek outstanding faculty whose research will contribute to this interdisciplinary mission. Areas of interest include cell and molecular biology, human physiology, biomedical technologies, computational and systems approaches, biomanufacturing, sustainable biological systems, and related areas of biomedical science and engineering. Candidates whose research crosses traditional disciplinary boundaries and creates connections between fundamental biological discovery and translational applications are particularly encouraged to apply. These areas reflect the Institute's publicly articulated research pillars while allowing candidates to bring forward their own scientific programs. Successful candidates will be expected to develop and maintain an innovative, externally funded research program; publish impactful scholarship; collaborate with investigators across disciplines; contribute to the scientific programs and intellectual community of the Trivedi Institute; and participate in the education and mentorship of students and trainees. The anticipated distribution of effort is approximately 80% research, 10% teaching, 9% administrative activities , and 1% service activities. Applicants should hold a PhD in a relevant field, including biological or biomedical sciences, life sciences, engineering or bioengineering, computational sciences, and related disciplines; an MD; or an equivalent doctoral degree and have appropriate postgraduate research training. Candidates at the Assistant Professor level should have 1-5 years of experience, demonstrate strong potential to develop an independent research program, obtain external research funding, and establish a record of impactful scholarship. Candidates at the Associate Professor level should have 6-10 years of experience and have an established record of independent research, peer-reviewed scholarship, and external research funding. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The successful candidate's primary academic appointment will be made in an appropriate department within the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine based on the candidate's scientific background, qualifications, and research interests. The position will be based at the Trivedi Institute for Space and Global Biomedicine, 450 Technology Drive, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Applicants should submit a curriculum vitae, cover letter, research statement describing current and future research directions, and names and contact information for three references / three letters of recommendation. Qualified applicants should apply through the University of Pittsburgh Talent Center at join.pitt.edu, requisition # 26006473 . The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006597&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology in Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant Professor of Psychology in Clinical Psychology (26006597) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant Professor of Psychology in Clinical Psychology (26006597) Job Description Assistant Professor of Psychology in Clinical Psychology Psychology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006597 ) The Department of Psychology at the University of Pittsburgh invites applications for one tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level in Clinical Psychology, pending budgetary approval, to begin Fall of 2027. We are seeking candidates with core training in Clinical Psychology whose research complements and builds upon our current research areas. Our primary interest is in candidates who do research on adult psychopathology. Those candidates who are license eligible are especially encouraged to apply. Candidates are encouraged to highlight how principles of transparency, openness, and/or generalizability have informed their approach to research. We also welcome candidates who can build our department-wide emphasis on varied cultures and perspectives by contributing research and training strengths in this area. The Psychology Department is committed to excellence in research and in teaching at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. Its 31 tenure-stream faculty offer five graduate training programs: Biological and Health, Clinical, Cognitive, Developmental, and Social, along with cross-program training opportunities. The interdisciplinary nature of psychological science is reflected in both faculty research interests and collaborations and training options afforded to graduate students. The deadline for submitting applications is November 13, 2026 . Applicants should assemble and submit a cover letter, CV, up to three papers, the names of three prospective referees, and statements of research, teaching, and service interests. The research, teaching, and service statements offer an opportunity to share your motivation, approach, experience, leadership, impact, and vision in each area, including how you would support the university’s mission ( https://www.plan.pitt.edu/ ). Other materials may be requested following the initial candidate review. For more information about the Department, including details about research emphasis in each of the five program areas, see http://www.psychology.pitt.edu . For more information about the position, please contact the co-chairs of the search committee, Anna Marsland ( marsland@pitt.edu ) and Kathryn Roecklein ( kroeck@pitt.edu ). The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer. Applicants should submit a cover letter, CV, statement of research and teaching interests, up to three papers, and the names of three prospective referees. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Teaching Statement, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26005927&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005927) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time (26005927) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Assistant - Full-Time Med-Radiation Oncology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26005927 ) The Department of Radiation Oncology at the UPMC Hillman Cancer Center , is recruiting outstanding basic/translational science faculty at the Assistant Professor level (appointment stream) . The Assistant Professor will be expected to develop an active research program focusing on basic and translational research in Thoracic Cancer. In this regard, you will be expected to be a member and work closely with other members of the Thoracic Cancer Disease Team and develop collaborations with members in HCC research programs. You will be expected to write short proposals about your research program, which will be used by the Center to seek funding from philanthropic and other sources, to help cover the Institute’s financial commitments to you. You will be expected to participate in the teaching and training of medical students and radiation oncology residents. As our department grows, we will be redefining the clinical, teaching, and research roles to meet the growing patient population. Teaching responsibilities include bedside teaching and precepting of medical trainees, and delivering 1-2 didactic lectures per year. The Assistant Professor will be expected to provide four days outpatient clinic per week at Hillman Cancer Center (“HCC”), or other locations as reasonably requested by the Department Chair. The Assistant Professor will participate in weekly Thoracic cancer disease team meetings and other activities as designated by the Department Chair. Successful candidates will have PhD, MD or equivalent in Biological Sciences or related field and an exceptional scientific research record encompassing basic and/or translational research using state-of-the-art approaches. Candidates for this position should have completed an accredited residency and be Board Certified or in the process of becoming Board Certified through the American Board of Radiology as well as having a demonstrated trajectory in basic or translational research. A competitive salary and research start-up package will be provided, as well as laboratory and office space within the state-of-the-art Hillman Cancer Center. Assistant Professor candidates shall have experience in cutting-edge cancer research in the field of Basic and/or Translational Research.  The ideal Candidate shall be an established independent investigator with interdisciplinary translational research in biology, significant publications, and extramural grant funding. The candidate will have a strong record in teaching and mentoring graduate students, postdoctoral fellows and junior faculty members. The candidate should have a strong commitment to collaborating with clinical and/or translational scientists and have the necessary skills for grant writing and producing peer-reviewed publications. The Department of Radiation Oncology has a mission of providing exceptional patient care, innovating next-generation research solutions to improve cancer patient outcomes, and educating future caregivers and researchers. The department includes multiple NIH-funded researchers at all levels with junior faculty funded on R03 and K08 awards as well as senior faculty leading R01 and P50 (SPORE) awards. Our department also has a strong mentorship program with regards to research training with current residents who have resident research grants through foundations such as ASCO and RSNA. Research faculty in the department are actively involved in multiple world-class research programs within Hillman including Cancer Biology, Cancer Immunology and Immunotherapy, Cancer Therapeutics, Cancer Virology, and Genome Stability Programs. Specialized resources within the Center for Precision Radiobiology led by faculty in the Department of Radiation Oncology include a stereotactic small animal irradiator as well as a dedicated radiochemistry laboratory for unsealed source radiopharmaceutical therapy research. The clinical department is actively involved in clinical trials through NRG Oncology, ECOG-ACRIN, Alliance, SWOG, and ETCTN trial networks as well as investigator-initiated trials with a dedicated radiation oncology disease team and clinical research which extends out to over 25 clinical sites. UPMC Hillman Cancer Center is the region’s only National Cancer Institute-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center and is one of the largest integrated community cancer networks in the United States. Backed by the collective strength of UPMC—which is ranked No. 15 for cancer care nationally by U.S. News & World Report—and the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine, UPMC Hillman Cancer Center has nearly 70 locations throughout Pennsylvania, Ohio, New York, and Maryland, with cancer centers and partnerships internationally. The more than 2,000 physicians, researchers, and staff are leaders in molecular and cellular cancer biology, cancer immunology, cancer virology, biobehavioral cancer control, cancer epidemiology, prevention, and therapeutics. UPMC Hillman Cancer Center is transforming cancer research, care, and prevention—one patient at a time. To apply for a position, go to Home | Talent Center: Careers at Pitt | University of Pittsburgh and search requisition #26005927. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Optional Attachments : Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006596&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty, Professor, Clinical Assistant-Part-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty, Professor, Clinical Assistant-Part-Time (26006596) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty, Professor, Clinical Assistant-Part-Time (26006596) Job Description Faculty, Professor, Clinical Assistant-Part-Time Dent Med-Restorative Dentistry/Comprehensive Care - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006596 ) The University of Pittsburgh School of Dental Medicine (UPSDM) is accepting applications for a part-time, appointment-stream faculty position at the academic rank of Clinical Instructor or Clinical Assistant Professor in the Department of Restorative Dentistry/Comprehensive Care. The salary will depend on experience and qualifications. The primary responsibilities of this position would be clinical instruction for dental students, scholarly activities, and service. Applicants must have a DDS or DMD degree from an accredited school. The applicant must have a Pennsylvania dental license and have significant clinical experience in restorative dentistry and comprehensive treatment planning. The University of Pittsburgh is a top-tier public research institution. The UPSDM is located on the university's main campus in Pittsburgh, contiguous with the other five health science schools. The School of Dental Medicine works as a key collaborative partner with the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC). UPMC is an internationally renowned academic medical center and healthcare enterprise. The robust infrastructure supports clinicians and educators with innovative clinical programs, biomedical research, and health sciences research, enabling discoveries that save lives and change the landscape of patient care. As part of the clinical practice and faculty of the University of Pittsburgh, the practitioner will have the opportunity to collaborate with clinicians, innovators, and investigators from around the world and become part of a vibrant community of healthcare providers dedicated to making a difference in their chosen field and in the lives of others. To apply, please go to join.pitt.edu, select faculty positions, and search 26006596 in the keyword search. Please upload a curriculum vitae, and a statement describing your interest in the position, qualifications, and experience. The search committee will begin reviewing applications upon receipt. Only applicants who appear best qualified will be invited for a personal interview. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Part-time temporary Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006385&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor Nuclear Medicine Radiologist",
      "description": "Job Description - Assistant/Associate/Professor Nuclear Medicine Radiologist (26006385) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Assistant/Associate/Professor Nuclear Medicine Radiologist (26006385) Job Description Assistant/Associate/Professor Nuclear Medicine Radiologist Med-Radiology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006385 ) UPMC/University of Pittsburgh, Department of Radiology Assistant/Associate Professor/Professor NT (Full-Time) Nuclear Medicine Division The Nuclear Medicine Division at UPMC and the University of Pittsburgh is currently accepting applications for an academic nuclear medicine physician. The Division of Nuclear Medicine encompasses a broad and comprehensive program of clinical and research activities with stateof- the-art facilities and exceptional faculty expertise to provide outstanding patient care, teaching, and research opportunities. UPMC is a world leader in research and development of both instrumentation and radiotracers. The first PET/CT scanner was invented at UPMC and we have over 100 radiolabeled compounds for human and animal use, including Pittsburgh Compound B (PiB). In addition, dedicated teaching and clinical experience are provided to all radiology residents in our ACGME accredited Diagnostic Radiology residency to ensure satisfaction of the ABR requirements. Our PET/CT fellowship also provides highly supervised clinical instruction in both PET and diagnostic CT interpretation. Duties for this position will consist of a mix of clinical, teaching, and academic responsibilities. The position will be based in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. Applicants must be board-eligible or board-certified by the American Board of Radiology or the American Board of Nuclear Medicine and be eligible for an unrestricted licensure in Pennsylvania. Completion of a Nuclear Medicine fellowship training is also required for ABR eligible/certified candidates. UPMC is a $21 billion global health enterprise with 90,000 employees headquartered in Pittsburgh, PA, including 4,900 employed physicians, more than 40 academic, community, and specialty hospitals, more than 700 doctors’ offices and outpatient sites, a health insurance services division, and international and commercial services. The Department of Radiology at UPMC is one of the largest academic radiology programs in the country. For more information, please visit our website: http://www.radiology.pitt.edu/ Minimum requirements: · MD degree, or equivalent · Completion of an ACGME accredited diagnostic radiology residency · Completion of a chest imaging fellowship · ABR certified or eligible · Eligible for licensure in Pennsylvania · Assistant Professor requires 1-5 year experience. · Associate Professor requires 6-10 year experience. · Professor requires 10 year experience. Interested applicants should submit a curriculum vitae and cover letter to requisition 26006385 on join.pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : The following PA Act 153 clearances and background checks are required prior to commencement of employment and as a condition of continued employment: PA State Police Criminal Record Check, FBI Criminal Record Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance. Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Optional Attachments : Cover Letter Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006150&lang=en": {
      "title": "Endourology-BPH ",
      "description": "Job Description - Endourology-BPH  (26006150) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Endourology-BPH  (26006150) Job Description Endourology-BPH Med-Urology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006150 ) The Department of Urology at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine and the University of Pittsburgh Medical Center (UPMC) is seeking a full-time faculty member. The position will include an appointment in the Department of Urology at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine as an Assistant or Associate Professor. Focused clinical responsibilities within a department of 40+ Clinical Urologists, will include attending duties in a large, integrated, multi-hospital clinical urology practice and educating students, residents, and fellows. The Candidate will be expected to provide endourologic services within a growing practice in the metropolitan Pittsburgh area. This position is best suited for a candidate with a focus on minimally invasive surgery, stone disease, and BPH. Minimum Requirements: The Candidate must have an M.D. in Urology with appropriate board certification/eligibility; experience in a large hospital service is beneficial. Eligibility for medical licensure or practice in Pennsylvania is required. Completion of an Endourological Society-accredited fellowship with a focus in Endourology or Combined Endourology is required. Qualified applicants are expected to have demonstrated excellence and commitment to patient care and experience with leading-edge diagnostic capabilities and delivery. Candidates at the Assistant Professor level should have 0 - 5 years of experience in clinical care and be committed to developing an academic career in clinical, transitional, or basic science research. Candidates at the Associate Professor level should have 6 - 9 years of experience and require evidence of significant educational or new clinical program development and/or a record of substantial clinical, translational, or basic science research. Recruitment is open until filled.  Salary commensurate with experience. Qualified applicants should apply via Talent Center under Requisition Number:  26006150 The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006159&lang=en": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (26006159) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Research Assistant Professor (26006159) Job Description Research Assistant Professor Med-Surgery - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006159 ) The Department of Surgery at the University of Pittsburgh is inviting applications for the faculty position of Research Assistant Professor. The faculty member will play a key role in collaborative research programs in the application of cutting-edge imaging technologies in regenerative medicine, diabetic peripheral neuropathy, and wound healing at the McGowan Institute of Regenerative Medicine (MIRM). QUALIFICATIONS: •    Must have a doctoral degree (Ph.D.) in Biology, Biochemistry or related field. Specific experience with the study of diabetic neuropathy, animal models, using cutting-edge imaging technologies such as confocal microscopy, laser speckled imaging (LSI), transmission electron microscopy, nail bed capillaroscopy, Akoya PhenoCycler spatial proteomics, and 10x Genomics Xenium spatial transcriptomics. •    [SS1.1]Specific experience with ex vivo skin bioreactor work is mandatory •    5+ years of research experience working in the academic research environment •    Must be willing to work with animals and human subjects •    Must be able to multitask and show interest in contributing to several projects ongoing in the Center. •    Tissue Nanotransfection experience preferred •    Electronic Lab Notebook (e.g., LabGuru) experience preferred RESPONSIBILITIES: The qualified scientist will play a major role in a dynamic program in basic and translational research in the application of cutting-edge-imaging technologies in regenerative medicine, diabetic peripheral neuropathy, and wound healing at the McGowan Institute of Regenerative Medicine (MIRM). The faculty member will be tasked with using a pre-clinical rodent model supported with advanced imaging including but not limited to MRI/ DTI based tractography of the brain function and for the detection of Diabetic Neuropathy as a function of Aging using Differential Tractography dMRI. As this is a supporting role, the faculty member will be required to partner with interdisciplinary scientists toward translational program building but will not be expected to have regular teaching or service responsibilities external to their research group. A successful candidate in this role will also actively support grant submissions and submit grants as PI. We offer a competitive academic salary, fringe benefits, and state-of-the-art facilities. The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. To apply, upload a current CV, cover letter, and letters of reference to requisition number: 26006159  at https:// www.join.pitt.edu The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006481&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty Professor - CIPE Director",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty Professor - CIPE Director (26006481) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty Professor - CIPE Director (26006481) Job Description Faculty Professor - CIPE Director Med-Immunology - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006481 ) The Department of Immunology at the University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine, in partnership with the UPMC Hillman Cancer Center (HCC), is seeking to expand its scope and depth via the recruitment of a Director of our newly established Center for Immunotherapeutics and Protein Engineering (CIPE) . We seek candidates for a tenured position at the Full Professor or Associate Professor level. We have a highly collaborative and collegial Department (32 faculty) that nucleates a larger interactive community (nearly 100 faculty). We support an exceptional Graduate Training Program, host two training grants, a robust weekly seminar series, and multiple retreats and programming events that collectively enable robust interactions among basic, translational and clinical immunologists. The Department of Immunology is ranked 6 th in the US and 9 th in the world (Research.com), and 2 nd in the US for NIH funding (Immunology ranked together with Microbiology and Virology; Blue Ridge). Our department also hosts The Center for Systems Immunology (CSI), which is focused on analysis and engineering of molecular and cellular networks that underlie immune processes in health and disease. The CIPE will be established in partnership with HCC, an NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center that was ranked as exceptional in the last review. The Department relocated in 2022 to a new start-of-the art research facility housed in a building listed on the historical registry. We host several research cores that are broadly used within the SOM that provide flow cytometry services and generate model systems using CRISPR-Cas9-mediated gene-targeting. The University of Pittsburgh is located in the Oakland and Shadyside sections of Pittsburgh; a safe, progressive, and affordable city with emerging technology in many spheres, that is well-endowed with cultural and public institutions and consistently ranked among the most livable cities in the US. The University offers an exciting research community that presently ranks as the seventh highest funded by the National Institutes of Health in the United States. The Pitt School of Medicine is ideally positioned for both basic and translational research. Startup package, salary and benefits will be highly competitive. The successful Associate/Full Professor candidate should be an international leader in immunotherapeutics and protein engineering, with a deep and broad understanding of i mmunology, and have a combined strong record of high impact publications and research funding (i.e. multiple current NIH R01 grants). The purpose of the CIPE is to (a) conduct cutting edge research in the development of novel immunotherapeutics and protein engineering strategies with a strong emphasis on translation, (b) utilize cutting-edge computational approaches to generate next generation immunotherapeutics, in close collaboration with CSI and other Pitt departments and faculty, (c) build a community around these themes by faculty recruitment and engagement with current faculty, and (d) manage the CIPE core, developing a system to evaluate proposals, and generate tool compounds for Pitt investigators. This Faculty Position will serve as the Director of the CIPE within the Department of Immunology. The candidate will collaborate with other researchers within UPMC Hillman Cancer Center, University of Pittsburgh, and throughout the national and international research community. The candidate will conduct wet and/or dry lab basic and/or translational research. The Candidate will hire and train their research staff within CIPE. Minimum requirements if an Associate Professor is hired are a PhD and/or MD (or equivalent) in the field of Immunology, I mmunotherapeutics, Protein Engineering or related field , and 5 years of Work Experience earned as an Assistant Professor. Minimum requirements if a Professor is hired are a PhD and/or MD (or equivalent) in the field of Immunology, I mmunotherapeutics, Protein Engineering or related field , and 5 years of Work Experience earned as an Associate Professor, and must currently have Tenure. Our long-term goal is to continue to grow an already strong department that will enhance opportunities for major research advances through deep cross-disciplinary collaborations. The successful applicant will be provided with a named, endowed chair and a generous start-up package for their lab, commensurate with their current rank and achievements, and resources to recruit two junior faculty and establish the CIPE core. Space will be provided within the Shadyside campus, in close proximity to the Department of Immunology within the UPMC Hillman Cancer Center. Applications will be considered on a rolling basis. The preferred application receipt date is December 1, 2026. However, we will consider applications at any time and this position will remain open to applicants until filled. To apply for this position, search for requisition #26006481 in Talent Center @ join.pitt.edu and complete a required on-line employment application. Click on “Find Positions” then “Faculty” and enter 26006481 into the keyword field, and click hour glass search button. Then select “Apply Now.” We require that you attach your CV, Cover Letter and Research Statement into your on-line application. Any enquiries can be sent to Dario Vignali, PhD, Chair, Department of Immunology, University of Pittsburgh School of Medicine, Assembly Building, 5051 Center Avenue, Pittsburgh, PA 15213. E-mail: immunologysearch@pitt.edu The University of Pittsburgh is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We require that you attach your CV, Cover Letter and Research Statement into your on-line application. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Other (see posting for additional details) Optional Attachments : Letters of Recommendation Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006593&lang=en": {
      "title": "Teaching Assistant Professor Neuroscience",
      "description": "Job Description - Teaching Assistant Professor Neuroscience (26006593) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Teaching Assistant Professor Neuroscience (26006593) Job Description Teaching Assistant Professor Neuroscience Neuroscience - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006593 ) The Department of Neuroscience at the University of Pittsburgh invites applications for a full-time Teaching Assistant Professor on a 9-month basis with an anticipated start date of August 15, 2027. The position is outside the tenure stream and is subject to annual review. Applicants must have a PhD in neuroscience or related field and previous teaching experience. Applicants will teach courses of the undergraduate curriculum (Undergraduate | Neuroscience | University of Pittsburgh), to be determined based on enrollment and need. Duties include teaching three 3-credit courses per term in the Fall and Spring terms, as well as departmental service. Other preferred qualifications include documented success in some or all of the following areas: formal training in pedagogy, teaching large undergraduate classes, use of evidence-based teaching practices, and ability to develop effective teaching strategies to support all students. The Department of Neuroscience is a highly interactive community situated on the Oakland campus of the University of Pittsburgh. We are dedicated to the mutual success of our faculty and students in our research, education, and outreach missions. The department and university nurture a strong teaching community with active efforts in teaching innovation and pedagogical research (https://www.neuroscience.pitt.edu). Pittsburgh is a city that is often voted “most livable” in the nation. We are dedicated to fostering a welcoming environment that nurtures success of all students https://www.wellbeing.pitt.edu/. To apply, candidates should submit the following PDF documents to Talent Center (join.pitt.edu): (a) letter of application, (b) CV, and (c) teaching portfolio (teaching statement, teaching materials, and teaching evaluations if available). At least three letters of reference should be sent directly by the recommenders to NROSCI1@pitt.edu. Applications will be reviewed starting January 4, 2027, and will continue until the position is filled. The appointment requires administrative and budgetary approval. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer. Summary of additional documents required: (a) teaching portfolio (teaching statement, teaching materials, and teaching evaluations if available). At least three letters of reference should be sent directly by the recommenders to NROSCI1@pitt.edu. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Cover Letter, Curriculum Vitae, Teaching Statement, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    },
    "https://cfopitt.taleo.net/careersection/pitt_faculty_external/jobdetail.ftl?job=26006675&lang=en": {
      "title": "Faculty.Professor.Research Assistant - Full-Time",
      "description": "Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Research Assistant - Full-Time (26006675) Go to the main content section. Office of Human Resources Why Work at Pitt Benefits Talent Center: Careers at Pitt Staff Positions Faculty Positions Postdoctoral Associate Positions Temporary Positions Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Faculty.Professor.Research Assistant - Full-Time (26006675) Job Description Faculty.Professor.Research Assistant - Full-Time Physics & Astronomy - Pennsylvania-Pittsburgh - ( 26006675 ) The LINCC Frameworks Team at the University of Pittsburgh is seeking to hire a full-time Project Scientist who will lead the development, testing and deployment of scalable analysis pipelines to enable science on data from the next generation of sky surveys, including the Vera C. Rubin Observatory’s Legacy Survey of Space and Time (LSST) and the Schmidt Observatory System. We seek computationally talented scientists with a background in astronomy who are ready to work with early adopters of these software platforms for this position, which will hold the rank of non-tenure-stream Research Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will have a Ph.D. in astrophysics or a closely related field and a strong computational background. The LINCC Frameworks team’s goal is to build analysis frameworks that can store, search, analyze and annotate data of the volume and complexity of next-generation data from surveys such as LSST. As a Project Scientist you will work with a team of software engineers to lead the development of one of the team’s focus areas such as scalable spatial analysis, time domain studies, minor planet observations, or photometric redshift measurements. In this position, you will lead the development and application of astronomical analyses using the software, work with external researchers to design and implement their analyses, and train and mentor junior staff. You will be integrally involved in producing, critiquing, improving, and disseminating results. Throughout this process, software engineers and research scientists involved in the project will develop example notebooks, facilitate testing for specific science use cases, and provide user support to ensure the scientific utility of the products. Successful candidates should be able to further their own research goals via the LINCC analysis frameworks. Interested candidates should provide a letter of application; a CV which includes lists of invited talks, of grant, telescope, and computing time applications, and of leadership and mentoring activities; a research statement; a publication list; and a brief statement of teaching and community-building interests and experience via www.join.pitt.edu by 15 December, 2026 to ensure full consideration; applications will continue to be considered on a rolling basis. Candidates should have 3 reference letters sent to Jeffrey Newman ( janewman@pitt.edu ) with the subject line LINCC. This position is part of the LINCC Frameworks program, https://lsstdiscoveryalliance.org/programs/lincc-frameworks/ , which includes multiple institutions: the University of Washington, Carnegie Mellon University, and the University of Pittsburgh. For questions please contact Professor Jeffrey Newman ( janewman@pitt.edu ) or Professor Michael Wood-Vasey ( wmwv@pitt.edu ). Compensation and Benefits The University provides a comprehensive package of fringe benefits including medical insurance, life insurance, disability insurance, a wellness program, and a retirement plan through TIAA. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer. The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran. Assignment Category : Full-time regular Bargaining Unit Eligibility : This position may be bargaining unit eligible Campus : Pittsburgh Child Protection Clearances : Not Applicable Required Attachments : Curriculum Vitae, Letters of Recommendation, Other (see posting for additional details) Talent Center: Careers at Pitt 200 S. Craig Street 100 Craig Hall Pittsburgh, PA 15260 412-624-7000 Contact OHR Resources Office of Human Resources Directions & Map to HR Office of Institutional Engagement and Wellbeing Required Workplace Postings Campus Safety Emergency Preparedness University Policies and Procedures E-Verify Stay Connected with Us The University of Pittsburgh is an equal opportunity employer / disability / veteran."
    }
  },
